-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part keel (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- THE SEAT LAYER of the keel: the questions of ss 2(4) to (6), 3, 4, 4A and 4B that a person in the seat would ask.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who holds, deals in, issues or offers securities, debentures or units, or who is, or is about to become, a director or
-- other officer, an employee or a substantial shareholder of a corporation. (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to market participants
-- and the Authority; there is never a seat for the Authority, the Minister or the Court.)
--
-- Every question is named `Under section N, ...`, carries @export and a question for the person, and answers MAYBE BOOLEAN with
-- JUST TRUE meaning yes, JUST FALSE meaning the text says no, and NOTHING meaning the text does not say (a number question answers NUMBER).
-- Inputs are plain facts, each with an @desc; the same fact keeps the same name and the same @desc in every module (PLAN.md section 7).
-- Where a rule needs "such other amount as the Authority may prescribe in place of the first amount", this layer asks no such question:
-- it takes the amounts as the Act states them, so a later prescription would change these answers (the underlying functions do take it).
-- A question that sits over several routes takes one yes/no per route; the question for each route is its own question above it.
--

§ `The keel questions: ss 2(4) to (6), 3, 4, 4A and 4B`

§§ `s 2: substantial shareholding`

@export Under section 2(4), do I have a substantial shareholding in the corporation?
GIVEN
    `the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have an interest (as section 4 treats it) in one or more voting shares, excluding treasury shares, in the corporation?
    `the total votes attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2(4), do I have a substantial shareholding in the corporation` MEANS
    `s 2(4) the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation` `the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` `the total votes attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in` `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation`

@export Under section 2(6), am I a substantial shareholder in the corporation?
GIVEN
    `the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have an interest (as section 4 treats it) in one or more voting shares, excluding treasury shares, in the corporation?
    `the total votes attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation?
    `the share capital of the corporation is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share capital of the corporation divided into two or more classes of shares?
    `the votes attached to the voting shares I have an interest in, in the class where my holding is largest` IS A NUMBER @desc In the class of voting shares where your holding is largest: how many votes are attached to the shares you have an interest in? (0 if the corporation has one class.)
    `the votes attached to all the voting shares in that class, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are attached to all the voting shares in that class, excluding treasury shares? (0 if the corporation has one class.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2(6), am I a substantial shareholder in the corporation` MEANS
    `s 2(6) the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation` ((`s 2(4) the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation` `the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` `the total votes attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in` `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) ((`s 2(5) the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation whose share capital has 2 or more classes` `the share capital of the corporation is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` (LIST (`Class of voting shares` WITH `the name of the class` IS "the class where my holding is largest", `the votes attached to the voting shares in the class that the person has an interest in` IS `the votes attached to the voting shares I have an interest in, in the class where my holding is largest`, `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the class, excluding treasury shares` IS `the votes attached to all the voting shares in that class, excluding treasury shares`))) EQUALS JUST TRUE)

§§ `s 3: associated person`

@export Under section 3(1)(a), is this person a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation?
GIVEN
    `the other person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
    `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director or secretary of the corporation?
    `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a related corporation of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "related corporation")?
    `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director or secretary of a corporation that is related to the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "related corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1)(a), is this person a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` MEANS
    `s 3(1)(a) the person is a director, secretary or related corporation of the corporation` `the other person is a corporation` `the person is a director or secretary of the corporation` `the person is a related corporation of the corporation` `the person is a director or secretary of a related corporation of the corporation`

@export Under section 3(1)(b), does this person have an agreement about voting power with me?
GIVEN
    `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter to which the reference relates the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation?
    `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other person have, or propose to enter into, with the person an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking, whether formal or informal, or express or implied?
    `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of it, may either of the two persons exercise, directly or indirectly, control the exercise of, or substantially influence the exercise of, any voting power attached to a share in the corporation?
    `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation?
    `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under it, may either of the two persons acquire from the other shares in the corporation, or be required to dispose of such shares in accordance with the other's directions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1)(b), does this person have an agreement about voting power with me` MEANS
    `s 3(1)(b) the person has an agreement about voting power with the other person` `the matter is the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` `the person has, or proposes to enter into with the other person, an agreement, arrangement, understanding or undertaking` `by reason of it either of them may exercise or control, or substantially influence, the voting power attached to a share in the corporation` `it is made with a view to controlling or influencing the composition of the board of directors, or the conduct of affairs, of the corporation` `under it either of them may acquire shares in the corporation from the other, or may be required to dispose of such shares as the other directs`

@export Under section 3(1)(c), is this person acting in concert with me?
GIVEN
    `the other person is acting, or proposes to act, in concert with the person in relation to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person acting, or proposing to act, in concert with the person in relation to the matter to which the reference relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1)(c), is this person acting in concert with me` MEANS
    `s 3(1)(c) the person is acting in concert with the other person` `the other person is acting, or proposes to act, in concert with the person in relation to the matter`

@export Under section 3(1)(d), is this person a fellow director or a trustee connected with me?
GIVEN
    `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter to which the reference relates a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation?
    `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director?
    `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it alleged, in proceedings under this Act, that the person was associated with another person at a particular time by being a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director?
    `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person alleging the association prove that the person alleged to be associated at that time knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the material particulars of the matter to which the proceedings relate?
    `the person is a trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee of a trust?
    `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the other person benefit, or is the other person capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1)(d), is this person a fellow director or a trustee connected with me` MEANS
    `s 3(1)(d) the person is a fellow director or a trustee connected with the other person` `the matter is a matter other than the extent of a power to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the voting power attached to voting shares in a corporation` `the person is a director of a corporation of which the other person is a director` `it is alleged in proceedings under this Act that the person was associated with the other person as a fellow director at a particular time` `the person alleging the association proves that the person at that time knew or ought reasonably to have known the material particulars of the matter` `the person is a trustee of a trust` `the other person benefits, or is capable of benefiting, from the trust otherwise than by reason of transactions entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money`

@export Under section 3(1)(e), does subsidiary legislation regard this person as associated with me?
GIVEN
    `subsidiary legislation made under this Act says the person is to be regarded as associated with the other person in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsidiary legislation made under this Act say that the person is to be regarded as associated with the other person in respect of the matter to which the reference relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1)(e), does subsidiary legislation regard this person as associated with me` MEANS
    `s 3(1)(e) subsidiary legislation regards the person as associated with the other person` `subsidiary legislation made under this Act says the person is to be regarded as associated with the other person in respect of the matter`

@export Under section 3(1)(f), is this person associated with me in some other way?
GIVEN
    `the other person is, or proposes to become, associated with the person, formally or informally, in any other way in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person, or does the other person propose to become, associated with the person, whether formally or informally, in any other way in respect of the matter to which the reference relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1)(f), is this person associated with me in some other way` MEANS
    `s 3(1)(f) the person is associated with the other person in another way` `the other person is, or proposes to become, associated with the person, formally or informally, in any other way in respect of the matter`

@export Under section 3(1)(g), have I acted with a view to becoming associated with this person?
GIVEN
    `the other person has entered into, or proposes to enter into, a transaction, or has done or proposes to do any other act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other person entered into, or does the other person propose to enter into, a transaction, or has the other person done, or does the other person propose to do, any other act or thing?
    `it is with a view to becoming associated with the person as referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it with a view to becoming associated with the person in a way referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) of section 3(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1)(g), have I acted with a view to becoming associated with this person` MEANS
    `s 3(1)(g) the other person has acted with a view to becoming associated with the person` `the other person has entered into, or proposes to enter into, a transaction, or has done or proposes to do any other act or thing` `it is with a view to becoming associated with the person as referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)`

@export Under section 3(1), is this person associated with me?
GIVEN
    `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading otherwise require a different meaning for the word?
    `this person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)? (Answer from the question for that paragraph.)
    `this person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)? (Answer from the question for that paragraph.)
    `this person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)? (Answer from the question for that paragraph.)
    `this person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)? (Answer from the question for that paragraph.)
    `this person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)? (Answer from the question for that paragraph.)
    `this person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)? (Answer from the question for that paragraph.)
    `this person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)? (Answer from the question for that paragraph.)
    `the association rests only on the circumstances in section 3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the association through paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) rest only on the circumstances in section 3(3) (advice or agency in a professional or business capacity, a customer's instructions, a take-over offer, or a proxy appointment)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(1), is this person associated with me` MEANS
    `s 3(1) the person is associated with the other person` `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` (IF `this person is within paragraph (a) of section 3(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within paragraph (b) of section 3(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within paragraph (c) of section 3(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within paragraph (d) of section 3(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within paragraph (e) of section 3(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within paragraph (f) of section 3(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within paragraph (g) of section 3(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `the association rests only on the circumstances in section 3(3)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 3(3), am I taken to be associated with this person by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) of section 3(1)?
GIVEN
    `one of the two persons (B) provides advice to, or acts on behalf of, the other (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the two persons (B) provide advice to, or act on behalf of, the other (A)?
    `B does so in the proper performance of the functions attaching to B's professional capacity or B's business relationship with A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B doing so in the proper performance of the functions attaching to B's professional capacity or to B's business relationship with A?
    `one of the two persons, a customer, gives specific instructions to the other (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the two persons, a customer, give specific instructions to the other (A)?
    `A's ordinary business includes dealing in capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A's ordinary business include dealing in capital markets products (as section 2(1) "dealing in capital markets products" has it)?
    `the instructions are to acquire shares on the customer's behalf in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the instructions to acquire shares on the customer's behalf in the ordinary course of that business?
    `one of the two persons has sent, or proposes to send, the other (A) a take-over offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of the two persons sent, or does one propose to send, the other (A) a take-over offer (as section 2(1) "take-over offer" has it)?
    `one of the two persons has made, or proposes to make, offers under a take-over announcement within the meaning of the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of the two persons made, or does one propose to make, offers under a take-over announcement, within the meaning of the Take-over Code?
    `it is in relation to shares held by A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in relation to shares held by A?
    `one of the two persons has appointed the other (A) to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of members, or of a class of members, of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of the two persons appointed the other (A) to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of members, or of a class of members, of a corporation?
    `the appointment was for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the appointment for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of A?
    `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the association through paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) of section 3(1) rest on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 3(3), am I taken to be associated with this person by virtue of paragraph (b), (c), (e) or (f) of section 3(1)` MEANS
    `s 3(3) the person is taken to be associated by virtue of subsection (1)(b), (c), (e) or (f)` (`s 3(3)(a) the circumstance is that one of the persons provides advice to, or acts for, the other in a professional or business capacity` `one of the two persons (B) provides advice to, or acts on behalf of, the other (A)` `B does so in the proper performance of the functions attaching to B's professional capacity or B's business relationship with A`) (`s 3(3)(b) the circumstance is that a customer gives specific instructions to a dealer to acquire shares` `one of the two persons, a customer, gives specific instructions to the other (A)` `A's ordinary business includes dealing in capital markets products` `the instructions are to acquire shares on the customer's behalf in the ordinary course of that business`) (`s 3(3)(c) the circumstance is that one of the persons has sent or proposes to send the other a take-over offer` `one of the two persons has sent, or proposes to send, the other (A) a take-over offer` `one of the two persons has made, or proposes to make, offers under a take-over announcement within the meaning of the Take-over Code` `it is in relation to shares held by A`) (`s 3(3)(d) the circumstance is that one of the persons has appointed the other as proxy or representative` `one of the two persons has appointed the other (A) to vote as a proxy or representative at a meeting of members, or of a class of members, of a corporation` `the appointment was for valuable consideration given by A or by an associate of A`) `the association rests on some ground other than the circumstances in paragraphs (a) to (d) of section 3(3)`

§§ `s 4: interest in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units`

@export Under section 4(1), do I have authority over the disposal of these securities, contracts or units?
GIVEN
    `the person has authority to dispose of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to dispose of the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the person has authority to exercise control over the disposal of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have authority (formal or informal, express or implied) to exercise control over the disposal of the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(1), do I have authority over the disposal of these securities, contracts or units` MEANS
    `s 4(1) the person has authority over the disposal of the thing` `the person has authority to dispose of the thing` `the person has authority to exercise control over the disposal of the thing`

@export Under section 4(3), am I treated as having an interest through a trust?
GIVEN
    `property held in trust consists of or includes the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does property held in trust consist of, or include, the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person know, or have reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest under the trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(3), am I treated as having an interest through a trust` MEANS
    `s 4(3) the person is treated as having an interest through a trust` `property held in trust consists of or includes the thing` `the person knows, or has reasonable grounds for believing, that the person has an interest under the trust`

@export Under section 4(4), am I treated as having an interest through a corporation I direct or control?
GIVEN
    `a corporation has, or is by section 4 treated as having, an interest in the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a corporation have, or is it by the provisions of section 4 treated as having, an interest in the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the corporation is, or its directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation, or are its directors, accustomed or under an obligation (formal or informal) to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the person?
    `the person has a controlling interest in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a controlling interest in the corporation? (The text does not define "controlling interest": say what you consider it to be.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(4), am I treated as having an interest through a corporation I direct or control` MEANS
    `s 4(4) the person is treated as having an interest through a corporation the person directs or controls` `a corporation has, or is by section 4 treated as having, an interest in the thing` `the corporation is, or its directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the person` `the person has a controlling interest in the corporation`

@export Under section 4(5), am I treated as having an interest through a corporation in which my associates and I hold 20 percent of the votes?
GIVEN
    `a corporation has, or is by section 4 (apart from subsection (5)) treated as having, an interest in the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a corporation have, or is it by the provisions of section 4 (apart from subsection (5)) treated as having, an interest in the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation that the person, the person's associates, or both are entitled to exercise or control` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation are the person, the person's associates (as subsection (6) has it), or the person and the associates together entitled to exercise or control the exercise of?
    `the total votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to the voting shares in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(5), am I treated as having an interest through a corporation in which my associates and I hold 20 percent of the votes` MEANS
    `s 4(5) the person is treated as having an interest through a corporation in which the person and associates hold 20% of the votes` `a corporation has, or is by section 4 (apart from subsection (5)) treated as having, an interest in the thing` `the votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation that the person, the person's associates, or both are entitled to exercise or control` `the total votes attached to the voting shares in the corporation`

@export Under section 4(6), is this person my associate for the purposes of section 4(5)?
GIVEN
    `the person is a subsidiary of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a subsidiary of the other person (as section 2(1) "subsidiary" has it)?
    `the person is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person accustomed, or under an obligation (formal or informal), to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme referred to in subsection (5)?
    `the person is a corporation that is, or a majority of whose directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions in relation to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation that is, or a majority of the directors of which are, accustomed or under an obligation (formal or informal) to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to that thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(6), is this person my associate for the purposes of section 4(5)` MEANS
    `s 4(6) the person is an associate of the other person for the purposes of subsection (5)` `the person is a subsidiary of the other person` `the person is accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the other person in relation to the thing` `the person is a corporation that is, or a majority of whose directors are, accustomed or under an obligation to act in accordance with the other person's directions in relation to the thing`

@export Under section 4(7), am I treated as having an interest in one of the listed circumstances?
GIVEN
    `the person has entered into a contract to purchase the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into a contract to purchase the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the person has a right to have the thing transferred to the person or to the person's order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a right (exercisable presently or in the future, and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not) to have the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme transferred to the person or to the person's order?
    `the right is by reason of the person having an interest under a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have that right by reason of having an interest under a trust?
    `the person has the right to acquire the thing under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have the right to acquire the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme under an option, whether the right is exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not?
    `the person has the right to acquire an interest in the thing under an option` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have the right to acquire an interest in the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme under an option, whether the right is exercisable presently or in the future and whether on the fulfilment of a condition or not?
    `the person is entitled to exercise, or to control the exercise of, a right attached to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person entitled to exercise, or to control the exercise of, a right attached to the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme?
    `the person is entitled only by reason of having been appointed a proxy or representative to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation or of a class of its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person entitled only by reason of having been appointed a proxy or representative to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation, or of a class of its members?
    `the person is the registered holder of the security or unit, or a party to the securities-based derivatives contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the registered holder of the security or of the unit in a collective investment scheme, or a party to the securities-based derivatives contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(7), am I treated as having an interest in one of the listed circumstances` MEANS
    `s 4(7) the person is treated as having an interest in one of the circumstances` (`s 4(7)(a) the person has entered into a contract to purchase the thing` `the person has entered into a contract to purchase the thing`) (`s 4(7)(b) the person has a right to have the thing transferred to the person or to the person's order` `the person has a right to have the thing transferred to the person or to the person's order` `the right is by reason of the person having an interest under a trust`) (`s 4(7)(c) the person has the right to acquire the thing, or an interest in it, under an option` `the person has the right to acquire the thing under an option` `the person has the right to acquire an interest in the thing under an option`) (`s 4(7)(d) the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right attached to the thing` `the person is entitled to exercise, or to control the exercise of, a right attached to the thing` `the person is entitled only by reason of having been appointed a proxy or representative to vote at a meeting of members of a corporation or of a class of its members` `the person is the registered holder of the security or unit, or a party to the securities-based derivatives contract`)

@export Under section 4(8), are these securities, contracts or units held jointly by me with another person?
GIVEN
    `the thing is held jointly by the person with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme held jointly by the person with another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(8), are these securities, contracts or units held jointly by me with another person` MEANS
    `s 4(8) the thing is held jointly by the person with another person` `the thing is held jointly by the person with another person`

@export Under section 4(10), is my interest to be disregarded?
GIVEN
    `the interest is that of a person who holds the thing as bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest that of a person who holds the security, securities-based derivatives contract or unit in a collective investment scheme as bare trustee?
    `the interest is that of a person whose ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest that of a person whose ordinary business includes the lending of money?
    `the person holds the interest only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold the interest only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money?
    `the person holds the interest by reason of holding an office that the regulations prescribe for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold the interest by reason of holding an office that is prescribed for this purpose? (The Act leaves the offices to the regulations.)
    `the interest is an interest of a company in its own securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest an interest of a company in its own securities?
    `the interest was purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interest purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G of the Companies Act 1967?
    `the interest is an interest the regulations prescribe, being that of a person, or of persons in a class of persons, the regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest a prescribed interest, being an interest of a person, or of persons included in a class of persons, as may be prescribed? (The Act leaves these to the regulations.)
    `the question arises for the purposes of Part 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the question arise for the purposes of Part 7 (disclosure of interests)?
    `the interest is in a securities-based derivatives contract the obligations under which are to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest in a securities-based derivatives contract the obligations under which are to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(10), is my interest to be disregarded` MEANS
    `s 4(10) the interest is to be disregarded` (`s 4(10)(a) the interest is that of a bare trustee` `the interest is that of a person who holds the thing as bare trustee`) (`s 4(10)(b) the interest is that of a lender holding it only as security` `the interest is that of a person whose ordinary business includes the lending of money` `the person holds the interest only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of business in connection with the lending of money`) (`s 4(10)(c) the interest is held by reason of holding a prescribed office` `the person holds the interest by reason of holding an office that the regulations prescribe for this purpose`) (`s 4(10)(d) the interest is a company's interest in its own securities bought under the Companies Act` `the interest is an interest of a company in its own securities` `the interest was purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G of the Companies Act 1967`) (`s 4(10)(e) the interest is a prescribed interest` `the interest is an interest the regulations prescribe, being that of a person, or of persons in a class of persons, the regulations prescribe`) (`s 4(10)(f) for Part 7, the interest is in a cash-settled securities-based derivatives contract` `the question arises for the purposes of Part 7` `the interest is in a securities-based derivatives contract the obligations under which are to be discharged by one party to the other at some future time by cash settlement only`)

@export Under section 4(11), is my interest to be disregarded by reason only of its remoteness, how it arose, or restraint?
GIVEN
    `the ground for disregarding the interest is its remoteness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one ground for disregarding the interest its remoteness?
    `the ground for disregarding the interest is the manner in which it arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one ground for disregarding the interest the manner in which it arose?
    `the ground for disregarding the interest is that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one ground for disregarding the interest that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction?
    `there is some other ground for disregarding the interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there any other ground for disregarding the interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4(11), is my interest to be disregarded by reason only of its remoteness, how it arose, or restraint` MEANS
    `s 4(11) the interest is to be disregarded by reason only of its remoteness, how it arose, or restraint` `the ground for disregarding the interest is its remoteness` `the ground for disregarding the interest is the manner in which it arose` `the ground for disregarding the interest is that the exercise of a right conferred by the interest is, or is capable of being made, subject to restraint or restriction` `there is some other ground for disregarding the interest`

@export Under section 4, do I have an interest in these securities, contracts or units?
GIVEN
    `the thing is a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme (as section 2(1) defines those)?
    `I have authority over the disposal of them (section 4(1))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under section 4(1), do I have authority to dispose of them or control their disposal?
    `I am treated as having an interest through a trust (section 4(3))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the answer to the question under section 4(3) yes?
    `I am treated as having an interest through a corporation I direct or control (section 4(4))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the answer to the question under section 4(4) yes?
    `I am treated as having an interest through a corporation in which my associates and I hold 20 percent of the votes (section 4(5))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the answer to the question under section 4(5) yes?
    `I am treated as having an interest in one of the circumstances in section 4(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the answer to the question under section 4(7) yes?
    `I hold them jointly with another person (section 4(8))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the answer to the question under section 4(8) yes?
    `my interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the answer to the question under section 4(10) yes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4, do I have an interest in these securities, contracts or units` MEANS
    `s 4 the person has an interest in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units` `the thing is a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme` (IF `I have authority over the disposal of them (section 4(1))` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `I am treated as having an interest through a trust (section 4(3))` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `I am treated as having an interest through a corporation I direct or control (section 4(4))` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `I am treated as having an interest through a corporation in which my associates and I hold 20 percent of the votes (section 4(5))` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `I am treated as having an interest in one of the circumstances in section 4(7)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `I hold them jointly with another person (section 4(8))` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `my interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

§§ `s 4A: specific classes of investors`

@export Under section 4A(1)(a), is this person an accredited investor?
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
    `the value of the individual's net personal assets other than the primary residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the individual's net personal assets other than the primary residence, in Singapore dollars?
    `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the estimated fair market value of the individual's primary residence, in Singapore dollars? (0 if none.)
    `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the outstanding amounts in respect of any credit facility that is secured by the residence, in Singapore dollars?
    `the value of the individual's financial assets, net of any related liabilities` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the individual's financial assets (deposits, investment products and the other assets in the definition of "financial asset"), net of any related liabilities, in Singapore dollars?
    `the individual's income in the preceding 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the individual's income in the preceding 12 months, in Singapore dollars?
    `the corporation has a most recent audited balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have an audited balance sheet (the most recent one is the one to use)?
    `the net assets shown by the most recent audited balance sheet` IS A NUMBER @desc What net assets does the most recent audited balance sheet of the corporation show, in Singapore dollars?
    `the corporation is required to prepare audited accounts regularly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation required to prepare audited accounts regularly?
    `the corporation has certified a balance sheet as giving a true and fair view of its state of affairs as of the date of the balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation certified a balance sheet as giving a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the corporation as of the date of the balance sheet?
    `the net assets shown by the certified balance sheet` IS A NUMBER @desc What net assets does the certified balance sheet show, in Singapore dollars?
    `the date of the certified balance sheet` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the certified balance sheet?
    `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
    `the Authority has prescribed the person as an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the person (or a class that includes the person) as an accredited investor?
    `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee of a trust that the Authority has prescribed for this purpose?
    `the person is acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting as trustee of that trust at the time in question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1)(a), is this person an accredited investor` MEANS
    `s 4A(1)(a) the person is an accredited investor` (`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(A) the individual's net personal assets exceed the amount` `the person is an individual` `the value of the individual's net personal assets other than the primary residence` `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence` FALSE 0) (`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) the individual's financial assets, net of related liabilities, exceed the amount` `the person is an individual` `the value of the individual's financial assets, net of any related liabilities` FALSE 0) (`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(C) the individual's income in the preceding 12 months is not less than the amount` `the person is an individual` `the individual's income in the preceding 12 months` FALSE 0) (`s 4A(1)(a)(ii) the corporation's net assets exceed the amount` `the person is a corporation` `the corporation has a most recent audited balance sheet` `the net assets shown by the most recent audited balance sheet` `the corporation is required to prepare audited accounts regularly` `the corporation has certified a balance sheet as giving a true and fair view of its state of affairs as of the date of the balance sheet` `the net assets shown by the certified balance sheet` `the date of the certified balance sheet` `the date asked` FALSE 0) (`s 4A(1)(a)(iii) the person is the trustee of a prescribed trust, when acting in that capacity` `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` `the person is acting in that capacity`) (`s 4A(1)(a)(iv) the person is a person the Authority has prescribed as an accredited investor` `the Authority has prescribed the person as an accredited investor`)

@export Under section 4A(1)(b), is this person an expert investor?
GIVEN
    `the person's business involves the acquisition and disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products, whether as principal or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person's business involve the acquisition and disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products, whether as principal or agent?
    `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee of a trust that the Authority has prescribed for this purpose?
    `the person is acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting as trustee of that trust at the time in question?
    `the Authority has prescribed the person as an expert investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the person (or a class that includes the person) as an expert investor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1)(b), is this person an expert investor` MEANS
    `s 4A(1)(b) the person is an expert investor` `the person's business involves the acquisition and disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products, whether as principal or agent` `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` `the person is acting in that capacity` `the Authority has prescribed the person as an expert investor`

@export Under section 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii), is this person the Government, a government body or a central-government entity?
GIVEN
    `the person is the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Government?
    `the person is a statutory board prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a statutory board prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `the person is an entity wholly and beneficially owned, directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity that is wholly and beneficially owned, whether directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country?
    `the person's principal activity is to manage its own funds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's principal activity to manage its own funds?
    `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of the central government of that country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's principal activity to manage the funds of the central government of that country (which may include its reserves and any pension or provident fund of that country)?
    `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of another entity wholly and beneficially owned by that central government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's principal activity to manage the funds (which may include the reserves of that central government and any pension or provident fund of that country) of another entity that is wholly and beneficially owned, whether directly or indirectly, by the central government of that country?
    `the person's funds are managed by an entity mentioned in sub-paragraph (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the person's funds managed by an entity mentioned in sub-paragraph (iii) (an entity wholly and beneficially owned by a central government whose principal activity is as described there)?
    `the person is a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore?
    `the person is a central government in a country other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a central government in a country other than Singapore?
    `the person is an agency of a central government in a country other than Singapore, incorporated or established in a country other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an agency (of a central government in a country other than Singapore) that is incorporated or established in a country other than Singapore?
    `the person is a multilateral agency, international organisation or supranational agency prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a multilateral agency, international organisation or supranational agency as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii), is this person the Government, a government body or a central-government entity` MEANS
    `s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii) the person is the Government, a government body or a central-government entity` `the person is the Government` `the person is a statutory board prescribed by regulations made under section 341` `the person is an entity wholly and beneficially owned, directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country` `the person's principal activity is to manage its own funds` `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of the central government of that country` `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of another entity wholly and beneficially owned by that central government` `the person's funds are managed by an entity mentioned in sub-paragraph (iii)` `the person is a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` `the person is a central government in a country other than Singapore` `the person is an agency of a central government in a country other than Singapore, incorporated or established in a country other than Singapore` `the person is a multilateral agency, international organisation or supranational agency prescribed by regulations made under section 341`

@export Under section 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv), is this person a licensed financial institution?
GIVEN
    `the person is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a bank that is licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
    `the person is a merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a merchant bank that is licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
    `the person is a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a finance company that is licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967?
    `the person is a company or co-operative society licensed under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a company or co-operative society that is licensed under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance business in Singapore?
    `the person is a company licensed under the Trust Companies Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a company licensed under the Trust Companies Act 2005?
    `the person is a holder of a capital markets services licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a holder of a capital markets services licence (as section 2(1) defines "capital markets services licence")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv), is this person a licensed financial institution` MEANS
    `s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv) the person is a licensed financial institution` `the person is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` `the person is a merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` `the person is a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967` `the person is a company or co-operative society licensed under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance business in Singapore` `the person is a company licensed under the Trust Companies Act 2005` `the person is a holder of a capital markets services licence`

@export Under section 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii), is this person an approved or recognised market institution?
GIVEN
    `the person is an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an approved exchange (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a recognised market operator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a recognised market operator (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is an approved clearing house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an approved clearing house (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a recognised clearing house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a recognised clearing house (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a licensed trade repository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a licensed trade repository (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a licensed foreign trade repository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a licensed foreign trade repository (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is an approved holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an approved holding company (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a Depository as defined in section 81SF` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a Depository as defined in section 81SF?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii), is this person an approved or recognised market institution` MEANS
    `s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii) the person is an approved or recognised market institution` `the person is an approved exchange` `the person is a recognised market operator` `the person is an approved clearing house` `the person is a recognised clearing house` `the person is a licensed trade repository` `the person is a licensed foreign trade repository` `the person is an approved holding company` `the person is a Depository as defined in section 81SF`

@export Under section 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii), is this person a foreign regulated entity, a pension fund or scheme, a bond dealer or a prescribed person?
GIVEN
    `the person is an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Singapore?
    `the person is regulated for the carrying on of any financial activity in that jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person regulated for the carrying on of any financial activity in that jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction?
    `that public authority exercises a function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under this Act or one of the listed Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that public authority exercise a function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under this Act, the Banking Act 1970, the Finance Companies Act 1967, the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022, the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970, the Insurance Act 1966, the Trust Companies Act 2005 or such other Act as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `the person is a pension fund, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a pension fund, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the person is a collective investment scheme, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a collective investment scheme (as section 2(1) defines it), whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person carries on the business of dealing in bonds with accredited investors or expert investors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person carry on the business of dealing in bonds with accredited investors or expert investors?
    `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee of a trust that the Authority has prescribed for this purpose?
    `the person is acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting as trustee of that trust at the time in question?
    `the Authority has prescribed the person as an institutional investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the person (or a class that includes the person) as an institutional investor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii), is this person a foreign regulated entity, a pension fund or scheme, a bond dealer or a prescribed person` MEANS
    `s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii) the person is a foreign regulated entity, a pension fund or scheme, a bond dealer or a prescribed person` `the person is an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` `the person is regulated for the carrying on of any financial activity in that jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction` `that public authority exercises a function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under this Act or one of the listed Acts` `the person is a pension fund, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` `the person is a collective investment scheme, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` `the person is an individual` `the person carries on the business of dealing in bonds with accredited investors or expert investors` `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` `the person is acting in that capacity` `the Authority has prescribed the person as an institutional investor`

@export Under section 4A(1)(c), is this person an institutional investor?
GIVEN
    `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii)? (Answer from the question for those limbs.)
    `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv)? (Answer from the question for those limbs.)
    `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii)? (Answer from the question for those limbs.)
    `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this person within s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii)? (Answer from the question for those limbs.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1)(c), is this person an institutional investor` MEANS
    `s 4A(1)(c) the person is an institutional investor` (IF `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `this person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 4A(1), is this person in this class of investor?
GIVEN
    `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading otherwise require a different meaning for the word?
    `the Authority has prescribed a modification of the definitions for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a modification of the definitions in section 4A(1) for the provision you are reading?
    `the class of investor asked about` IS A `Class of investor` @desc Which class of investor is asked about?
    `the investor is an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the investor an accredited investor (the answer to the question under section 4A(1)(a))?
    `the investor is an expert investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the investor an expert investor (the answer to the question under section 4A(1)(b))?
    `the investor is an institutional investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the investor an institutional investor (the answer to the question under section 4A(1)(c))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4A(1), is this person in this class of investor` MEANS
    `s 4A(1) the person is in the class of investor` `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` `the Authority has prescribed a modification of the definitions for the provision` `the class of investor asked about` (IF `the investor is an accredited investor` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `the investor is an expert investor` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE) (IF `the investor is an institutional investor` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

@export Under section 4A(1A), what is the value of my primary residence to count in my net personal assets?
GIVEN
    `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the estimated fair market value of the individual's primary residence, in Singapore dollars?
    `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the outstanding amounts in respect of any credit facility that is secured by the residence, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 4A(1A), what is the value of my primary residence to count in my net personal assets` MEANS
    `s 4A(1A) the value of the individual's primary residence counted in net personal assets` `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence`

@export Under section 4B, does this Act apply to this person in respect of the activities?
GIVEN
    `a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 is in force in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 in force in respect of the person?
    `the activities carried out by the person are regulated under, and authorised by, that section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the activities the person carries out regulated under, and authorised by, section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 4B, does this Act apply to this person in respect of the activities` MEANS
    `s 4B this Act applies to the person in respect of the activities` `a transitional approval or transitional licence mentioned in section 66 of the Commodity Trading Act 1992 is in force in respect of the person` `the activities carried out by the person are regulated under, and authorised by, that section`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sfaa (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- THE SEAT LAYER for Part 7 (disclosure of interests) and Part 8 (the Securities Industry Council and take-over offers).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director or other officer, an employee or a substantial shareholder of a corporation
-- (including the holding company of a group that has listed members), or who holds, deals in, issues or offers securities, debentures or units,
-- asking, on facts they can state, what the Act requires or lets them do: what they must disclose and by when, and what follows if they do not.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the Act is addressed to market participants and the Authority, so the individual is whoever holds an interest in securities or offers them.)
-- There is no seat for the Authority, the Minister, the Council or the Court: their powers appear only as what they mean to the individual
-- (a summons, an order, an action for a civil penalty).
--
-- Nothing here is new law. Each question calls one layer-1 function (or two or three of them, for a definition built from its paragraphs) and passes it the
-- facts the person states. No rule is restated. Every question is named "Under section N, ..." and asks in the direction its layer-1 function answers.
-- JUST TRUE is yes. JUST FALSE is no, in the text's own words. NOTHING is "the text does not say" (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
--
-- INPUTS. A fact keeps one name and one @desc across the question set, and across the family where the plan fixes a name (PLAN section 7.1 and 7.2).
-- Where the person has to say which public holidays fall in the days counted, they give a list of dates (sfa-periods counts business days as the days
-- other than Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays).
-- Amounts and dates the Act leaves to the Authority (the prescribed form of a notice, what the Authority has prescribed) are not asked: the seat covers
-- when a notice is owed and by when, not whether its form was right. Where an answer turns on a fact the Act hands to the Authority or the court
-- (an exemption, an extension, whether it appears to the Authority), the person states the fact.

§ `Securities and Futures Act 2001 -- the individual's questions on Part 7 and Part 8`


§§ `Part 7 Division 1: the corporation`

-- Whether Division 1 reaches the corporation is asked once, here; the later questions take the answer as a plain fact.

-- s 130(2). Paragraph (a) is a company with shares listed; paragraph (b) a corporation other than a company with a primary listing. The input for the listing in (a) is the fixed name `the corporation is listed on an approved exchange`.
@export Under section 130(2), is this corporation one to which Division 1 applies?
GIVEN
    `the corporation is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
    `the corporation is listed on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation listed on an approved exchange (as section 2(1) defines "approved exchange")?
    `the corporation is a collective investment scheme constituted as a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a collective investment scheme constituted as a corporation?
    `the listing is a primary listing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the listing on the approved exchange a primary listing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 130(2), is this corporation one to which Division 1 applies` MEANS
    `s 130(2) the body is a corporation for the purposes of Division 1` (`s 130(2)(a) the body is a company listed on an approved exchange` `the corporation is a company` `the corporation is listed on an approved exchange`) (`s 130(2)(b) the body is a corporation other than a company with a primary listing` `the corporation is a company` `the corporation is a collective investment scheme constituted as a corporation` `the corporation is listed on an approved exchange` `the listing is a primary listing`)

-- s 131(6). The Authority's power to extend the time is its own (section 131(6)); the question is what the extension means for the person who applied. Applies to any notice under Division 1.
@export Under section 131(6), what is the last day for my notice, if the Authority has extended the time on my application?
GIVEN
    `the last day for my notice under the section` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for your notice under the section, before any extension?
    `the Authority has extended the time on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority extended the time for your notice on your application?
    `the last day to which the Authority has extended the time` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day to which the Authority has extended the time?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 131(6), what is the last day for my notice, if the Authority has extended the time on my application` MEANS
    `s 131(6) the last day for giving the notice, as extended on the person's application` `the last day for my notice under the section` `the Authority has extended the time on my application` `the last day to which the Authority has extended the time`

§§ `Part 7 Division 1: a director or chief executive officer (sections 133 and 134)`

-- Asked only by someone who is, or is about to become, a director or chief executive officer of the corporation.

-- s 133(1).
@export Under section 133(1), must I give the corporation written notice of my interests as a director or chief executive officer?
GIVEN
    `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2))?
    `I am a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
    `I am a chief executive officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the chief executive officer of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "chief executive officer")?
    `the corporation is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
    `the kind of thing I hold or have an interest in` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which of these do you hold, or have an interest in, as a director or chief executive officer?
    `I hold or have an interest in the matter, or the particulars of my interest have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, or have an interest in, the matter, or have the particulars of it changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 133(1), must I give the corporation written notice of my interests as a director or chief executive officer` MEANS
    `s 133(1) the director or chief executive officer must give the corporation written notice of the matter` `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` `I am a director of the corporation` `I am a chief executive officer of the corporation` `the corporation is a company` `the kind of thing I hold or have an interest in` `I hold or have an interest in the matter, or the particulars of my interest have changed`

-- s 133(3)(b)(i). 2 business days after the day section 130(6) takes you to have been aware (the earlier of the two days you give).
@export Under section 133(3)(b)(i), what is the last day for my notice of a change in my interests?
GIVEN
    `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you actually become aware of the fact or occurrence that gives rise to the notice?
    `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which you, or your officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of your affairs?
    `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which of the days counted are public holidays in Singapore? (a list of dates; leave it empty if there are none)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 133(3)(b)(i), what is the last day for my notice of a change in my interests` MEANS
    `s 133(3)(b)(i) the last day for the notice of a change` `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted`

-- s 133(3)(b)(ii). 2 business days after the day you became a director or chief executive officer, or became a holder of, or acquired an interest in, the matter.
@export Under section 133(3)(b)(ii), what is the last day for my first notice of my interests?
GIVEN
    `the day I became a director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `the day I became a holder of, or acquired an interest in, the matter` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become a holder of, or acquire an interest in, the matter?
    `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which of the days counted are public holidays in Singapore? (a list of dates; leave it empty if there are none)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 133(3)(b)(ii), what is the last day for my first notice of my interests` MEANS
    `s 133(3)(b)(ii) the last day for any other notice` `the day I became a director or chief executive officer` `the day I became a holder of, or acquired an interest in, the matter` `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted`

-- s 133(4)(a). A family member is a spouse, or a child below 21 (section 133(6)); the age limit is read as applying to children, not to the spouse (NOTES.md, fork A2).
@export Under section 133(4)(a), am I deemed to have my family member's interest in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVEN
    `that person's relation to me` IS A `Family relation` @desc What is that person's relation to you?
    `that person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is that person, in years?
    `that person is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `that person holds or has an interest in those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person hold, or have an interest in, those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 133(4)(a), am I deemed to have my family member's interest in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` MEANS
    `s 133(4)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to have the family member's interest` (`s 133(6) "family member" the person is a family member` `that person's relation to me` `that person's age in years`) `that person is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation` `that person holds or has an interest in those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`

-- s 134(1).
@export Under section 134(1), am I guilty of an offence for failing to notify the corporation, or for giving it false or misleading information?
GIVEN
    `the kind of thing I hold or have an interest in` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which of these do you hold, or have an interest in, as a director or chief executive officer?
    `I contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene section 133(1) in respect of the matter?
    `I contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene section 133(3) in respect of the notice?
    `my contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your contravention intentional or reckless?
    `in purported compliance I provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance, did you provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `I knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or were you reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 134(1), am I guilty of an offence for failing to notify the corporation, or for giving it false or misleading information` MEANS
    `s 134(1) the director or chief executive officer is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` `the kind of thing I hold or have an interest in` `I contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` `I contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` `my contravention was intentional or reckless` `in purported compliance I provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` `I knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`

§§ `Part 7 Division 1: a substantial shareholder (sections 135 to 137B)`

-- Asked only by someone who is, or has been, a substantial shareholder in the corporation, or who holds or acquires shares for one.

-- s 135(1).
@export Under section 135(1), must I give the corporation written notice of particulars of my voting shares?
GIVEN
    `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2))?
    `I am a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a substantial shareholder in the corporation (as section 2(6) defines it)?
    `I was a substantial shareholder in the corporation but have ceased to be one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a substantial shareholder in the corporation but have you ceased to be one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 135(1), must I give the corporation written notice of particulars of my voting shares` MEANS
    `s 135(1) the person must give the corporation written notice of particulars of the voting shares` `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` `I am a substantial shareholder in the corporation` `I was a substantial shareholder in the corporation but have ceased to be one`

-- s 135(2)(b).
@export Under section 135(2)(b), what is the last day for my notice of particulars of my voting shares?
GIVEN
    `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you actually become aware of the fact or occurrence that gives rise to the notice?
    `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which you, or your officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of your affairs?
    `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which of the days counted are public holidays in Singapore? (a list of dates; leave it empty if there are none)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 135(2)(b), what is the last day for my notice of particulars of my voting shares` MEANS
    `s 135(2)(b) the last day for the notice` `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted`

-- s 136(1).
@export Under section 136(1), must I give the corporation written notice of a change in the percentage level of my interests?
GIVEN
    `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2))?
    `I am a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a substantial shareholder in the corporation (as section 2(6) defines it)?
    `the percentage level of my interests before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the percentage level of your interests in the voting shares before the change? (as a percentage)
    `the percentage level of my interests after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage level of your interests in the voting shares after the change? (as a percentage)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 136(1), must I give the corporation written notice of a change in the percentage level of my interests` MEANS
    `s 136(1) the substantial shareholder must give the corporation written notice of the change in the percentage level` `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` `I am a substantial shareholder in the corporation` `the percentage level of my interests before the change` `the percentage level of my interests after the change`

-- s 136(1).
@export Under section 136(1), what is the last day for my notice of a change in the percentage level of my interests?
GIVEN
    `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you actually become aware of the fact or occurrence that gives rise to the notice?
    `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which you, or your officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of your affairs?
    `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which of the days counted are public holidays in Singapore? (a list of dates; leave it empty if there are none)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 136(1), what is the last day for my notice of a change in the percentage level of my interests` MEANS
    `s 136(1) the last day for the notice` `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted`

-- s 137(1).
@export Under section 137(1), must I give the corporation written notice that I have ceased to be a substantial shareholder?
GIVEN
    `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2))?
    `I cease to be a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you cease to be a substantial shareholder in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137(1), must I give the corporation written notice that I have ceased to be a substantial shareholder` MEANS
    `s 137(1) the person who ceases to be a substantial shareholder must give the corporation written notice` `the corporation is one to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies` `I cease to be a substantial shareholder in the corporation`

-- s 137(1).
@export Under section 137(1), what is the last day for my notice that I have ceased to be a substantial shareholder?
GIVEN
    `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you actually become aware of the fact or occurrence that gives rise to the notice?
    `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which you, or your officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of your affairs?
    `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which of the days counted are public holidays in Singapore? (a list of dates; leave it empty if there are none)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 137(1), what is the last day for my notice that I have ceased to be a substantial shareholder` MEANS
    `s 137(1) the last day for the notice` `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted`

-- s 137A.
@export Under section 137A, must I take reasonable steps to ensure that the person acting for me gives me notice of an acquisition or disposal?
GIVEN
    `I have authorised another person to hold, acquire or dispose of voting shares, or an interest in voting shares, in the corporation on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you authorised another person to hold, acquire or dispose of voting shares, or an interest in voting shares, in the corporation on your behalf?
    `the other person has effected an acquisition or disposal on my behalf that will or may give rise to a duty to give notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other person effected an acquisition or disposal on your behalf that will or may give rise to a duty to give notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137A, must I take reasonable steps to ensure that the person acting for me gives me notice of an acquisition or disposal` MEANS
    `s 137A the person must take reasonable steps to ensure that the other person notifies the person` `I have authorised another person to hold, acquire or dispose of voting shares, or an interest in voting shares, in the corporation on my behalf` `the other person has effected an acquisition or disposal on my behalf that will or may give rise to a duty to give notice`

-- s 137B.
@export Under section 137B, must I give the other person notice of my acquisition or disposal of voting shares?
GIVEN
    `I hold voting shares in a corporation in which another person has an interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold voting shares in a corporation in which another person has an interest?
    `I have acquired or disposed of any of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you acquired or disposed of any of those shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137B, must I give the other person notice of my acquisition or disposal of voting shares` MEANS
    `s 137B the person must give the other person a notice of the acquisition or disposal` `I hold voting shares in a corporation in which another person has an interest` `I have acquired or disposed of any of those shares`

§§ `Part 7 Division 1: what follows if I do not (sections 137D to 137G)`

-- Asked only by someone who has failed to give a notice, or has been asked for information, or is an officer of a corporation that has failed to announce one.

-- s 137D(1).
@export Under section 137D(1), am I guilty of an offence for failing to notify as a substantial shareholder, or for giving false or misleading information?
GIVEN
    `I contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B?
    `my contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your contravention intentional or reckless?
    `in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B I provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B, did you provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `I knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or were you reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137D(1), am I guilty of an offence for failing to notify as a substantial shareholder, or for giving false or misleading information` MEANS
    `s 137D(1) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` `I contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B` `my contravention was intentional or reckless` `in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B I provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` `I knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`

-- s 137D(1). The fine is the same for an individual and a corporation ($250,000); an individual can also be imprisoned (layer 1 records both).
@export Under section 137D(1), what is the most I can be fined on conviction?
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 137D(1), what is the most I can be fined on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 137D(1) the penalty on conviction` `the person is an individual` `the person is a corporation`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (`penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` OF p)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 137E(1).
@export Under section 137E(1), may the court make an order against me for failing to notify as a substantial shareholder?
GIVEN
    `I am or have been a substantial shareholder in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, a substantial shareholder in the corporation?
    `I have failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137?
    `the Authority has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority applied to the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137E(1), may the court make an order against me for failing to notify as a substantial shareholder` MEANS
    `s 137E(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` `I am or have been a substantial shareholder in the corporation` `I have failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137` `the Authority has applied to the court`

-- s 137F(5).
@export Under section 137F(5), must I comply with the corporation's notice asking about my interest in its voting shares?
GIVEN
    `the corporation has issued me a notice under section 137F(1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued you a notice under section 137F(1), (2) or (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137F(5), must I comply with the corporation's notice asking about my interest in its voting shares` MEANS
    `s 137F(5) the person must comply with the notice` `the corporation has issued me a notice under section 137F(1), (2) or (3)`

-- s 137F(8).
@export Under section 137F(8), am I guilty of an offence for not complying with the corporation's notice, or for giving false or misleading information?
GIVEN
    `I contravened section 137F(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene section 137F(5)?
    `my contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your contravention intentional or reckless?
    `in purported compliance with section 137F(5) I provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137F(5), did you provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `I knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or were you reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137F(8), am I guilty of an offence for not complying with the corporation's notice, or for giving false or misleading information` MEANS
    `s 137F(8) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (8)` `I contravened section 137F(5)` `my contravention was intentional or reckless` `in purported compliance with section 137F(5) I provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` `I knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`

-- s 137F(8).
@export Under section 137F(8), what is the most I can be fined on conviction?
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 137F(8), what is the most I can be fined on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 137F(8) the penalty on conviction` `the person is an individual` `the person is a corporation`
    WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (`penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` OF p)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 137G(5)(d). The first input is the fixed name `I am an officer of the corporation`; it is passed for the officer description in section 137G(5).
@export Under section 137G(5)(d), am I, as an officer, guilty of an offence because the corporation failed to announce a notice, or announced false information, intentionally or recklessly?
GIVEN
    `I am an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "officer")?
    `I purport to act as an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you purport to act as a director, member of the committee of management, chief executive officer, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the corporation?
    `the corporation has committed an offence under section 137G(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation committed an offence under section 137G(3) or (4)?
    `I caused the corporation to contravene section 137G(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause the corporation to contravene section 137G(1)?
    `I announced or disseminated, or permitted or authorised the announcement or dissemination of, information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you announce or disseminate, or permit or authorise the announcement or dissemination of, information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `I announced or disseminated, or permitted or authorised the announcement or dissemination of, the information in contravention of section 137G(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you announce or disseminate, or permit or authorise the announcement or dissemination of, the information in contravention of section 137G(2)?
    `I acted intentionally or recklessly, or with knowledge that the information was false or misleading in a material particular or reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act intentionally or recklessly, or with knowledge that the information was false or misleading in a material particular or reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137G(5)(d), am I, as an officer, guilty of an offence because the corporation failed to announce a notice, or announced false information, intentionally or recklessly` MEANS
    `s 137G(5)(d) the officer is guilty of an offence for acting intentionally or recklessly` `I am an officer of the corporation` `I purport to act as an officer of the corporation` `the corporation has committed an offence under section 137G(3) or (4)` `I caused the corporation to contravene section 137G(1)` `I announced or disseminated, or permitted or authorised the announcement or dissemination of, information that is false or misleading in a material particular` `I announced or disseminated, or permitted or authorised the announcement or dissemination of, the information in contravention of section 137G(2)` `I acted intentionally or recklessly, or with knowledge that the information was false or misleading in a material particular or reckless as to whether it was`

§§ `Part 7 Division 2: business trusts (sections 137H to 137R)`

-- Asked only by someone who is a substantial unitholder of a business trust, or a director, chief executive officer or voting shareholder of its trustee-manager.

-- s 137H.
@export Under section 137H, is this business trust one to which Division 2 applies?
GIVEN
    `the trust is a registered business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a registered business trust?
    `any or all of the units in the trust are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any or all of the units in the trust listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange?
    `the trust is a recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a recognised business trust?
    `the listing is a primary listing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the listing on the approved exchange a primary listing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137H, is this business trust one to which Division 2 applies` MEANS
    `s 137H the trust is a business trust within Division 2` (`s 137H(2) the trust is a registered business trust for the purposes of Division 2` `the trust is a registered business trust` `any or all of the units in the trust are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange`) (`s 137H(3) the trust is a recognised business trust for the purposes of Division 2` `the trust is a recognised business trust` `any or all of the units in the trust are listed for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange` `the listing is a primary listing`)

-- s 137J(1). Section 137J(1) applies sections 135 to 137B to the substantial unitholder as though the corporation were the trustee-manager, shares were units and a substantial shareholder were a substantial unitholder. Layer 1 models that by passing the unitholder's facts to the section 135 function (sfaa-div2-trust, section 137J); the section 135 function is called for a person who is a substantial unitholder now (the third argument, "ceased", is FALSE), because section 137J(1) reaches only "a person who is a substantial unitholder" (NOTES.md, fork C1).
@export Under section 137J(1), must I give the trustee-manager written notice of particulars of my voting units?
GIVEN
    `the trust is a registered business trust or recognised business trust within section 137H` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a registered business trust or recognised business trust as section 137H(2) and (3) read those words for Division 2 (the answer to the question under section 137H)?
    `I am a substantial unitholder in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a substantial unitholder in the business trust (as section 2(1) defines "substantial unitholder")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137J(1), must I give the trustee-manager written notice of particulars of my voting units` MEANS
    IF `s 137J(1) sections 135 to 137B apply to the substantial unitholder` `the trust is a registered business trust or recognised business trust within section 137H` `I am a substantial unitholder in the business trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `s 135(1) the person must give the corporation written notice of particulars of the voting shares` TRUE `I am a substantial unitholder in the business trust` FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who is a substantial unitholder of a registered business trust or recognised business trust"

-- s 137J(1).
@export Under section 137J(1), what is the last day for my notice to the trustee-manager of particulars of my voting units?
GIVEN
    `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you actually become aware of the fact or occurrence that gives rise to the notice?
    `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which you, or your officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of your affairs?
    `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which of the days counted are public holidays in Singapore? (a list of dates; leave it empty if there are none)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 137J(1), what is the last day for my notice to the trustee-manager of particulars of my voting units` MEANS
    `s 135(2)(b) the last day for the notice` `the day I actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which I, or my officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays in Singapore in the days counted`

-- s 137N(1).
@export Under section 137N(1), must I give the trustee-manager written notice of my interests as a director or chief executive officer?
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust (as Division 2 reads those words)?
    `I am a director of the trustee-manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the trustee-manager (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
    `I am a chief executive officer of the trustee-manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the chief executive officer of the trustee-manager (as section 2(1) defines "chief executive officer")?
    `I hold or have an interest in the matter, or the particulars of my interest have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, or have an interest in, the matter, or have the particulars of it changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137N(1), must I give the trustee-manager written notice of my interests as a director or chief executive officer` MEANS
    `s 137N(1) the director or chief executive officer must give the trustee-manager written notice of the matter` `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` `I am a director of the trustee-manager` `I am a chief executive officer of the trustee-manager` `I hold or have an interest in the matter, or the particulars of my interest have changed`

-- s 137P(1).
@export Under section 137P(1), must I give the trustee-manager written notice of the change in the percentage of my interest in its voting shares?
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust (as Division 2 reads those words)?
    `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the trustee-manager before the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the percentage of your interest in the voting shares in the trustee-manager before the relevant time? (as a percentage)
    `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the trustee-manager after the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage of your interest in the voting shares in the trustee-manager after the relevant time? (as a percentage)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137P(1), must I give the trustee-manager written notice of the change in the percentage of my interest in its voting shares` MEANS
    `s 137P(1) the person must give the trustee-manager written notice of the change in the percentage of interest` `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the trustee-manager before the relevant time` `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the trustee-manager after the relevant time`

§§ `Part 7 Division 3: real estate investment trusts (sections 137S to 137ZC)`

-- Asked only by someone who is a substantial unitholder of a real estate investment trust, or a director, chief executive officer or voting shareholder of its responsible person.

-- s 137S(2).
@export Under section 137S(2), is this scheme a real estate investment trust for the purposes of Division 3?
GIVEN
    `the scheme is a collective investment scheme that is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a collective investment scheme that is a trust?
    `the scheme invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme invest primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes?
    `any or all of the units in the scheme are listed by way of a primary listing for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any or all of the units in the scheme listed by way of a primary listing for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137S(2), is this scheme a real estate investment trust for the purposes of Division 3` MEANS
    `s 137S(2) the scheme is a real estate investment trust` `the scheme is a collective investment scheme that is a trust` `the scheme invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` `any or all of the units in the scheme are listed by way of a primary listing for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange`

-- s 137U(1). Section 137U(1) applies sections 135 to 137B to the substantial unitholder of a real estate investment trust as though the corporation were the responsible person; layer 1 models that as for section 137J(1).
@export Under section 137U(1), must I give the responsible person written notice of particulars of my voting units?
GIVEN
    `the trust is a real estate investment trust within section 137S` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a real estate investment trust as section 137S(2) reads those words for Division 3 (the answer to the question under section 137S(2))?
    `I am a substantial unitholder in the real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a substantial unitholder in the real estate investment trust (as section 2(1) defines "substantial unitholder")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137U(1), must I give the responsible person written notice of particulars of my voting units` MEANS
    IF `s 137U(1) sections 135 to 137B apply to the substantial unitholder` `the trust is a real estate investment trust within section 137S` `I am a substantial unitholder in the real estate investment trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `s 135(1) the person must give the corporation written notice of particulars of the voting shares` TRUE `I am a substantial unitholder in the real estate investment trust` FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who is a substantial unitholder of a real estate investment trust"

-- s 137Y(1).
@export Under section 137Y(1), must I give the responsible person written notice of my interests as a director or chief executive officer?
GIVEN
    `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the responsible person for a real estate investment trust?
    `I am a director of the responsible person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the responsible person (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
    `I am a chief executive officer of the responsible person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the chief executive officer of the responsible person (as section 2(1) defines "chief executive officer")?
    `I hold or have an interest in the matter, or the particulars of my interest have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold, or have an interest in, the matter, or have the particulars of it changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137Y(1), must I give the responsible person written notice of my interests as a director or chief executive officer` MEANS
    `s 137Y(1) the director or chief executive officer must give the responsible person written notice of the matter` `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust` `I am a director of the responsible person` `I am a chief executive officer of the responsible person` `I hold or have an interest in the matter, or the particulars of my interest have changed`

-- s 137ZA(1).
@export Under section 137ZA(1), must I give the responsible person written notice of the change in the percentage of my interest in its voting shares?
GIVEN
    `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the responsible person for a real estate investment trust?
    `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the percentage of your interest in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time? (as a percentage)
    `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage of your interest in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time? (as a percentage)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137ZA(1), must I give the responsible person written notice of the change in the percentage of my interest in its voting shares` MEANS
    `s 137ZA(1) the person must give the responsible person written notice of the change in the percentage of interest` `the body is the responsible person for a real estate investment trust` `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the responsible person before the relevant time` `the percentage of my interest in the voting shares in the responsible person after the relevant time`

§§ `Part 7 Division 4: the civil penalty (sections 137ZD to 137ZG)`

-- Asked only by someone the Authority may pursue for a civil penalty for what is described in section 137ZD(1).

-- s 137ZD(1). Paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) are worked out in layer 1 from the facts you state; the Authority's own judgment ("it appears to the Authority") and the Public Prosecutor's consent are facts you supply.
@export Under section 137ZD(1), may the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action against me for a civil penalty?
GIVEN
    `the provision I contravened under section 137ZD(1)(a)` IS A `s 137ZD(1)(a) provision` @desc Which of the provisions listed in section 137ZD(1)(a) did you contravene? (choose the last entry if none of them)
    `I contravened it intentionally or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you contravene it intentionally or recklessly?
    `the provision I purported to comply with under section 137ZD(1)(b)` IS A `s 137ZD(1)(b) provision` @desc With which of the provisions listed in section 137ZD(1)(b) did you purport to comply? (choose the last entry if none of them)
    `in purported compliance I provided, announced or disseminated information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance, did you provide, announce or disseminate information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `I knew the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or were you reckless as to whether it was?
    `I am an officer of a corporation to which Division 1 applies, of a trustee-manager to which Division 2 applies, or of a responsible person to which Division 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer of a corporation to which Division 1 applies, of a trustee-manager to which Division 2 applies, or of a responsible person to which Division 3 applies?
    `I committed an act referred to in section 137G(5)(a), (b) or (c), 137R(5)(a), (b) or (c) or 137ZC(5)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commit an act referred to in section 137G(5)(a), (b) or (c), 137R(5)(a), (b) or (c) or 137ZC(5)(a), (b) or (c)?
    `I acted intentionally or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act intentionally or recklessly?
    `it appears to the Authority that I have done an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Authority that you have done an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)?
    `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137ZD(1), may the Authority, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action against me for a civil penalty` MEANS
    `s 137ZD(1) the Authority may bring an action in a court for an order for a civil penalty` `my act` `it appears to the Authority that I have done an act referred to in section 137ZD(1)(a), (b) or (c)` `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action`
    WHERE
        `my act` MEANS
            IF (`s 137ZD(1)(a) the person intentionally or recklessly contravened a provision the paragraph lists` `the provision I contravened under section 137ZD(1)(a)` `I contravened it intentionally or recklessly` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 137ZD(1)(b) the person gave false or misleading information in purported compliance with a provision the paragraph lists` `the provision I purported to comply with under section 137ZD(1)(b)` `in purported compliance I provided, announced or disseminated information that is false or misleading in a material particular` `I knew the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 137ZD(1)(c) the officer intentionally or recklessly committed an act referred to in the paragraph` `I am an officer of a corporation to which Division 1 applies, of a trustee-manager to which Division 2 applies, or of a responsible person to which Division 3 applies` `I committed an act referred to in section 137G(5)(a), (b) or (c), 137R(5)(a), (b) or (c) or 137ZC(5)(a), (b) or (c)` `I acted intentionally or recklessly` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 137ZD(2). Not less than $50,000 and not more than $2 million.
@export Under section 137ZD(2), is a civil penalty of this amount within the limits the section sets?
GIVEN
    `the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137ZD(2), is a civil penalty of this amount within the limits the section sets` MEANS
    `s 137ZD(2) the amount of the civil penalty is within the limits` `the amount of the civil penalty, in Singapore dollars`

-- s 137ZE(1). Barred after 6 years from the date of the act, or once convicted, or once acquitted other than because the charge was withdrawn.
@export Under section 137ZE(1), is an action against me for a civil penalty barred?
GIVEN
    `the day of the act` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act done?
    `the day the action is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 137ZD commenced?
    `I have been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against me for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against you for the act?
    `I have been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against me for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against you for the act?
    `I was acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge against you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 137ZE(1), is an action against me for a civil penalty barred` MEANS
    `s 137ZE(1) the action must not be commenced` `the day of the act` `the day the action is commenced` `I have been convicted in criminal proceedings instituted against me for the act` `I have been acquitted in criminal proceedings instituted against me for the act` `I was acquitted because of the withdrawal of the charge`

§§ `Part 8: the Securities Industry Council and take-over offers (sections 138 to 140)`

-- The Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers is not encoded: what the Code requires is not answered here. Asked only by someone the Council summons, a lawyer holding a client's document, or a party to a take-over offer.

-- s 138(4). The Act does not say here what happens if you do not comply (NOTES.md, what the text does not answer).
@export Under section 138(4), may the Securities Industry Council summon me to give evidence on oath or affirmation or to produce a document or material?
GIVEN
    `the Securities Industry Council is exercising its functions in an enquiry into a matter or thing related to the securities industry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Securities Industry Council, in the exercise of its functions, enquiring into a matter or thing related to the securities industry?
    `the evidence, document or material is necessary for the purpose of the enquiry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence, document or material necessary for the purpose of the enquiry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 138(4), may the Securities Industry Council summon me to give evidence on oath or affirmation or to produce a document or material` MEANS
    `s 138(4) the Securities Industry Council may summon the person to give evidence on oath or affirmation or produce a document or material` `the Securities Industry Council is exercising its functions in an enquiry into a matter or thing related to the securities industry` `the evidence, document or material is necessary for the purpose of the enquiry`

-- s 138(5).
@export Under section 138(5), is my document protected from production and from the taking of possession under section 138(4)?
GIVEN
    `I am an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893?
    `the document contains a privileged communication made by or to me in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document contain a privileged communication made by or to you in that capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 138(5), is my document protected from production and from the taking of possession under section 138(4)` MEANS
    `s 138(5) the document is protected from production and from the taking of possession under subsection (4)` `I am an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` `the document contains a privileged communication made by or to me in that capacity`

-- s 138(6).
@export Under section 138(6), must I give the name and address of the person for whom or by whom the privileged communication was made?
GIVEN
    `I am an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893?
    `I refuse to produce the document referred to in section 138(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you refuse to produce the document referred to in section 138(5)?
    `I know the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 138(6), must I give the name and address of the person for whom or by whom the privileged communication was made` MEANS
    `s 138(6) the person must give the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made` `I am an advocate and solicitor, or a legal counsel referred to in section 128A of the Evidence Act 1893` `I refuse to produce the document referred to in section 138(5)` `I know the name and address of the person to whom or by or on behalf of whom the communication was made`

-- s 139(4). What the Code's provisions say is not in the Act and is not answered here.
@export Under section 139(4), must I comply with the provisions of the Take-over Code?
GIVEN
    `I am a party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 139(4), must I comply with the provisions of the Take-over Code` MEANS
    `s 139(4) the person must comply with the provisions of the Take-over Code` `I am a party concerned in a take-over offer or a matter connected with one`

-- s 139(8). JUST FALSE here is the Act's own no: the failure "does not of itself render that party liable to criminal proceedings" (but it may be relied on in proceedings, section 139(8), and the Council may sanction it, section 139(9)).
@export Under section 139(8), does my failure to observe the Take-over Code of itself make me liable to criminal proceedings?
GIVEN
    `I have failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 139(8), does my failure to observe the Take-over Code of itself make me liable to criminal proceedings` MEANS
    `s 139(8) the failure of itself renders the party liable to criminal proceedings` `I have failed to observe a provision of the Take-over Code`

-- s 140(3). Layer 1 holds the two prohibitions and the offence; the facts you state are worked into "you contravene" here.
@export Under section 140(3), am I guilty of an offence for announcing, or making, a take-over offer I do not intend or cannot perform?
GIVEN
    `I have no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer?
    `I give notice or publicly announce that I intend to make a take-over offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you give notice or publicly announce that you intend to make a take-over offer?
    `I have no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that I will be able to perform my obligations if the take-over offer is accepted or approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that you will be able to perform your obligations if the take-over offer is accepted or approved, as the case may be?
    `I make a take-over offer, or give notice or publicly announce that I intend to make one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a take-over offer, or give notice or publicly announce that you intend to make one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 140(3), am I guilty of an offence for announcing, or making, a take-over offer I do not intend or cannot perform` MEANS
    `s 140(3) the person is guilty of an offence under section 140` `I contravene section 140(1)` `I contravene section 140(2)`
    WHERE
        `I contravene section 140(1)` MEANS (`s 140(1) the person must not give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make a take-over offer` `I have no intention to make an offer in the nature of a take-over offer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `I give notice or publicly announce that I intend to make a take-over offer`
        `I contravene section 140(2)` MEANS (`s 140(2) the person must not make a take-over offer or give notice or publicly announce that the person intends to make one` `I have no reasonable or probable grounds for believing that I will be able to perform my obligations if the take-over offer is accepted or approved` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `I make a take-over offer, or give notice or publicly announce that I intend to make one`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sfab (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text) -- THE SEAT LAYER for Part 12 (ss 196 to 238).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who is, or is about to become, a director or other officer, an employee or a substantial shareholder of a corporation, or who holds, deals in,
-- issues or offers securities, debentures or units, asking on facts they can state what Part 12 bars, excepts or lets be done to them, and what follows.
-- (Assumed, not ruled: the lead's reading of the seat.) There is no seat for the Authority, the Minister or the court: their powers appear only as what they mean to the person.
--
-- THIN LAYER. Every question is one `DECIDE` over one layer-1 function of the sfab modules and restates no rule. Its inputs are that function's own inputs, worded as
-- the person would be asked. An input that is another section's answer (marked "the answer under section N" in its name) stays JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING, so that
-- "I do not know" can be said; the question for that other section is asked first, and its answer is carried across.
-- READING AN ANSWER. JUST TRUE is "yes" to the question as it is worded; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say",
-- never "no" (NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING). A bar is titled as a bar ("does my conduct contravene ..."), a permission as a permission, a defence as a defence.
-- Every question begins "Under section N," so that it cannot share a name with a question of another part.

§ `Division 1: false trading, market manipulation, false statements and continuous disclosure (ss 196 to 204)`

@export Under section 197(1), does my conduct contravene the bar on acts done to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading?
GIVEN
    `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct?
    `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose, or one of your purposes, for it to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market?
    `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose, or one of your purposes, for it to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market?
    `the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading is presumed under section 197(3) and the presumption is not rebutted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading presumed under section 197(3), and has the presumption not been rebutted under section 197(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(1), does my conduct contravene the bar on acts done to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading` IS
    `s 197(1) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on conduct done to create a false or misleading appearance` `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market` `the purpose or one of the purposes is to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market` `the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading is presumed under section 197(3) and the presumption is not rebutted`

@export Under section 197(1A), does my conduct contravene the bar on acts that create a false or misleading appearance, done knowingly or recklessly?
GIVEN
    `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do a thing, cause a thing to be done or engage in a course of conduct?
    `the thing creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market, or with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the thing create, or is it likely to create, a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market, or with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market?
    `the person knows that the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that doing the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance?
    `the person is reckless as to whether the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reckless as to whether doing the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(1A), does my conduct contravene the bar on acts that create a false or misleading appearance, done knowingly or recklessly` IS
    `s 197(1A) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on conduct that creates a false or misleading appearance knowingly or recklessly` `the person did a thing, caused a thing to be done or engaged in a course of conduct` `the thing creates, or is likely to create, a false or misleading appearance of active trading in capital markets products on an organised market, or with respect to the market for, or the price of, capital markets products traded on an organised market` `the person knows that the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance` `the person is reckless as to whether the thing will create, or will be likely to create, that false or misleading appearance`

@export Under section 197(2), does my conduct contravene the bar on maintaining, inflating or depressing the market price?
GIVEN
    `the person maintained, inflated, depressed or caused fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you maintain, inflate, depress or cause fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products?
    `the person did so by a purchase or sale that does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership (the answer under section 197(5))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so by means of a purchase or sale of capital markets products that does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 197(5), or NOTHING if not known)
    `the person did so by a fictitious transaction or device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so by a fictitious transaction or device?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(2), does my conduct contravene the bar on maintaining, inflating or depressing the market price` IS
    `s 197(2) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on maintaining, inflating or depressing the market price` `the person maintained, inflated, depressed or caused fluctuations in the market price of capital markets products` `the person did so by a purchase or sale that does not involve a change in the beneficial ownership (the answer under section 197(5))` `the person did so by a fictitious transaction or device`

@export Under section 197(3)(b), is my purpose presumed to be to create a false or misleading appearance because I offered to sell and a matching offer to purchase was made?
GIVEN
    `the person makes or causes to be made an offer to sell the capital markets products at a specified price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make, or cause to be made, an offer to sell the capital markets products at a specified price?
    `the person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made or caused to be made, or do you propose to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same number, or substantially the same number, of the capital markets products at a price that is substantially the same as the first-mentioned price?
    `the person knows that another person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know that another person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same number, or substantially the same number, of the capital markets products at a price that is substantially the same as the first-mentioned price?
    `the other person is a person associated with the person (as section 3 reads)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person associated with you? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 3(1), or NOTHING if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(3)(b), is my purpose presumed to be to create a false or misleading appearance because I offered to sell and a matching offer to purchase was made` IS
    `s 197(3)(b) the person's purpose is presumed by reason of an offer to sell matched by an offer to purchase` `the person makes or causes to be made an offer to sell the capital markets products at a specified price` `the person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` `the person knows that another person has made or caused to be made, or proposes to make or cause to be made, an offer to purchase the same or substantially the same number of the capital markets products at substantially the same price` `the other person is a person associated with the person (as section 3 reads)`

@export Under section 197(4), is the presumption of my purpose rebutted?
GIVEN
    `the presumption under section 197(3) arises (the answer under section 197(3))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 197(3) answer in your case? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the defendant establishes that the purpose or purposes was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you establish that the purpose or purposes for which you did the act was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading in the capital markets products on the organised market?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 197(4), is the presumption of my purpose rebutted` IS
    `s 197(4) the presumption under subsection (3) is rebutted` `the presumption under section 197(3) arises (the answer under section 197(3))` `the defendant establishes that the purpose or purposes was not, or did not include, the purpose of creating a false or misleading appearance of active trading`

@export Under section 198(1), do my transactions contravene the bar on market manipulation in a corporation's securities?
GIVEN
    `the number of transactions in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation that the person effected, took part in, was concerned in or carried out` IS A NUMBER @desc How many transactions in securities, or securities-based derivatives contracts, of the corporation did you effect, take part in, be concerned in or carry out, directly or indirectly?
    `the transactions have, or are likely to have, the effect of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the transactions have, or are they likely to have, the effect of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts on an organised market?
    `the person acted with the intent to induce other persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or of a related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act with the intent to induce other persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or of a related corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 198(1), do my transactions contravene the bar on market manipulation in a corporation's securities` IS
    `s 198(1) the person's transactions contravene the bar on market manipulation in securities of a corporation` `the number of transactions in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation that the person effected, took part in, was concerned in or carried out` `the transactions have, or are likely to have, the effect of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the price on an organised market` `the person acted with the intent to induce other persons to subscribe for, purchase or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of the corporation or of a related corporation`

@export Under section 199, does my statement contravene the bar on false or misleading statements?
GIVEN
    `the person made a statement, or disseminated information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a statement, or disseminate information?
    `the statement or information is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement or information false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the statement or information is likely to induce other persons to subscribe for securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement or information is likely to induce other persons to subscribe for securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme?
    `the statement or information is likely to induce the sale or purchase of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme by other persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement or information is likely to induce the sale or purchase of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme by other persons?
    `the statement or information is likely to have the effect, whether significant or otherwise, of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the market price of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement or information is likely to have the effect, whether significant or otherwise, of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the market price of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme?
    `when the person made the statement or disseminated the information, the person did not care whether it was true or false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that when you made the statement or disseminated the information, you did not care whether it was true or false?
    `when the person made the statement or disseminated the information, the person knew or ought reasonably to have known that it was false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that when you made the statement or disseminated the information, you knew or ought reasonably to have known that it was false or misleading in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 199, does my statement contravene the bar on false or misleading statements` IS
    `s 199 the person's statement or information contravenes the bar on false or misleading statements` `the person made a statement, or disseminated information` `the statement or information is false or misleading in a material particular` `the statement or information is likely to induce other persons to subscribe for securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` `the statement or information is likely to induce the sale or purchase of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme by other persons` `the statement or information is likely to have the effect, whether significant or otherwise, of raising, lowering, maintaining or stabilising the market price of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` `when the person made the statement or disseminated the information, the person did not care whether it was true or false` `when the person made the statement or disseminated the information, the person knew or ought reasonably to have known that it was false or misleading in a material particular`

@export Under section 200(1), does my conduct contravene the bar on fraudulently inducing a person to deal?
GIVEN
    `the person induced or attempted to induce another person to deal in capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you induce, or attempt to induce, another person to deal in capital markets products?
    `the person made or published a statement, promise or forecast that the person knew or ought reasonably to have known to be misleading, false or deceptive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you made or published a statement, promise or forecast that you knew or ought reasonably to have known to be misleading, false or deceptive?
    `the person dishonestly concealed material facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you dishonestly conceal material facts?
    `the person recklessly made or published a statement, promise or forecast that is misleading, false or deceptive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you recklessly made or published a statement, promise or forecast that is misleading, false or deceptive?
    `the person recorded or stored in, or by means of, a mechanical, electronic or other device information that the person knew to be false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you recorded or stored in, or by means of, a mechanical, electronic or other device information that you knew to be false or misleading in a material particular?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 200(1), does my conduct contravene the bar on fraudulently inducing a person to deal` IS
    `s 200(1) the person's conduct contravenes the bar on fraudulently inducing a person to deal` `the person induced or attempted to induce another person to deal in capital markets products` `the person made or published a statement, promise or forecast that the person knew or ought reasonably to have known to be misleading, false or deceptive` `the person dishonestly concealed material facts` `the person recklessly made or published a statement, promise or forecast that is misleading, false or deceptive` `the person recorded or stored in, or by means of, a mechanical, electronic or other device information that the person knew to be false or misleading in a material particular`

@export Under section 200(2), do I have the defence to a contravention constituted by recording or storing information?
