@export Under section 222, do sections 218(2) and 219(2) not apply to my redemption of units in a collective investment scheme?
GIVEN
    `the act is the redemption of units in a collective investment scheme by a trustee or manager under a trust deed relating to the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act the redemption of units in a collective investment scheme by a trustee or manager under a trust deed relating to that scheme?
    `the redemption is in accordance with a buy-back covenant contained or deemed to be contained in the trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the redemption in accordance with a buy-back covenant contained or deemed to be contained in the trust deed?
    `the price is required by the trust deed to be calculated, so far as is reasonably practicable, by reference to the underlying value of the assets less the liabilities of the scheme to which the units relate and any reasonable charge for purchasing the units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the price one that the trust deed requires to be calculated, so far as is reasonably practicable, by reference to the underlying value of the assets less (a) any liabilities of the scheme to which the units relate and (b) any reasonable charge for purchasing the units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 222, do sections 218(2) and 219(2) not apply to my redemption of units in a collective investment scheme` IS
    `s 222 sections 218(2) and 219(2) do not apply to the redemption of units` `the act is the redemption of units in a collective investment scheme by a trustee or manager under a trust deed relating to the scheme` `the redemption is in accordance with a buy-back covenant contained or deemed to be contained in the trust deed` `the price is required by the trust deed to be calculated, so far as is reasonably practicable, by reference to the underlying value of the assets less the liabilities of the scheme to which the units relate and any reasonable charge for purchasing the units`

@export Under section 228, do I not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) merely because I am aware of my own intentions or activities?
GIVEN
    `the individual entered into the transaction or agreement merely because the individual is aware that the individual proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter into the transaction or agreement in relation to securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units merely because you are aware that you propose to enter into, or have previously entered into, one or more transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 228, do I not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) merely because I am aware of my own intentions or activities` IS
    `s 228 the individual does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) merely because the individual is aware of the individual's own intentions or activities` `the individual entered into the transaction or agreement merely because the individual is aware that the individual proposes to enter into, or has previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to those securities, contracts or units`

@export Under section 230(1), do I as a licence holder or representative not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by an unsolicited transaction for a principal?
GIVEN
    `the person is the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder?
    `the holder or representative entered into the transaction on behalf of the principal under a specific instruction by the principal that was not solicited by the holder or representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter into the transaction or agreement on behalf of another person (the principal) under a specific instruction by the principal to enter into that transaction or agreement which was not solicited by you?
    `the holder or representative has not given advice to the principal in relation to the transaction or otherwise sought to procure the principal's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not given any advice to the principal in relation to the transaction or agreement, or otherwise sought to procure the principal's instructions to enter into it?
    `the principal is an associate of the holder or representative (as section 3 reads)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the principal your associate? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE from the question under section 3(1), or NOTHING if not known)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 230(1), do I as a licence holder or representative not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by an unsolicited transaction for a principal` IS
    `s 230(1) the holder or representative does not contravene section 218(2) or 219(2) by an unsolicited transaction for a principal` `the person is the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products, or a representative of such a holder` `the holder or representative entered into the transaction on behalf of the principal under a specific instruction by the principal that was not solicited by the holder or representative` `the holder or representative has not given advice to the principal in relation to the transaction or otherwise sought to procure the principal's instructions` `the principal is an associate of the holder or representative (as section 3 reads)`

@export Under section 231(1), do I have the parity of information defence to a contravention by dealing or procuring?
GIVEN
    `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or 219(2) because the person entered into, or procured another person to enter into, a transaction or agreement at a time when certain information was in the person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for a contravention of section 218(2) or 219(2) because you entered into, or procured another person to enter into, a transaction or agreement at a time when certain information was in your possession?
    `the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of its having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the information came into your possession solely as a result of the information having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)?
    `the other party to the transaction or agreement knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before entering into it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the other party to the transaction or agreement knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before entering into the transaction or agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 231(1), do I have the parity of information defence to a contravention by dealing or procuring` IS
    `s 231(1) the person has the parity of information defence to the contravention by dealing or procuring` `the proceedings are for a contravention of section 218(2) or 219(2) because the person entered into, or procured another person to enter into, a transaction or agreement at a time when certain information was in the person's possession` `the information came into the person's possession solely as a result of its having been made known as referred to in section 215(b)(i)` `the other party to the transaction or agreement knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the information before entering into it`

