§ `Division 4: civil penalty and civil liability (ss 232 to 236)`

@export Under section 232(2), what is the most I can be ordered to pay as a civil penalty, in dollars?
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the person gained as a result of the contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that you gained as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the person avoided as a result of the contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that you avoided as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 232(2), what is the most I can be ordered to pay as a civil penalty, in dollars` IS
    `s 232(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` (`s 232(2)(a) three times the profit gained or the loss avoided` `the amount of the profit that the person gained as a result of the contravention` `the amount of the loss that the person avoided as a result of the contravention`) `s 232(2)(b) the fixed amount in the cap`

@export Under section 232(3), what is the least civil penalty a court can order me to pay, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 232(3), what is the least civil penalty a court can order me to pay, in dollars` IS
    `s 232(3) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` FALSE  -- an individual is not "a corporation"; the other case is the $100,000 floor of section 232(3)(a)

@export Under section 233(1), is a civil penalty action against me barred because 6 years have passed since the contravention?
GIVEN
    `the date of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you contravene the provision of Part 12?
    `the date the action under section 232 is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 232 commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 233(1), is a civil penalty action against me barred because 6 years have passed since the contravention` IS
    `s 233(1) the action under section 232 is barred because 6 years have expired from the date of the contravention` `the date of the contravention` `the date the action under section 232 is commenced`

@export Under section 234(1), am I liable to pay compensation to the claimant?
GIVEN
    `the contravening person has acted in contravention of a provision of Part 12 (the answer under the section contravened)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under the section of Part 12 that you are said to have contravened answer in your case? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the contravening person had gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention?
    `the claimant had been dealing contemporaneously (the answer under section 234(1)(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 234(1)(a) answer for the claimant? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
    `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference in price (the answer under section 234(1)(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 234(1)(b) answer for the claimant? (JUST TRUE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 234(1), am I liable to pay compensation to the claimant` IS
    `s 234(1) the contravening person is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` `the contravening person has acted in contravention of a provision of Part 12 (the answer under the section contravened)` `the contravening person had gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention` `the claimant had been dealing contemporaneously (the answer under section 234(1)(a))` `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference in price (the answer under section 234(1)(b))`

@export Under section 234(2), what is the amount of compensation I am liable to pay the claimant under section 234(1), in dollars?
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in section 234(1)(b)?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by you or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
    `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum amount recoverable under section 234(6) for the contravention?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 234(2), what is the amount of compensation I am liable to pay the claimant under section 234(1), in dollars` IS
    `s 234(2) the amount of compensation under subsection (1)` `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant referred to in subsection (1)(b)` `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` `the maximum amount recoverable (the answer under section 234(6))`

@export Under section 235(1), is an action for compensation under section 234 barred against me unless the court gives permission?
GIVEN
    `the contravention resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contravention result in you gaining a profit or avoiding a loss?
    `the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action under section 234 brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against you for the same contravention?
    `the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action under section 234 brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 against you for the same contravention?
    `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given permission for the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 235(1), is an action for compensation under section 234 barred against me unless the court gives permission` IS
    `s 235(1) no action under section 234 may be brought without the permission of court` `the contravention resulted in the contravening person gaining a profit or avoiding a loss` `the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings under Part 12 against the contravening person for the same contravention` `the action under section 234 is brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 against the contravening person for the same contravention` `the court has given permission`

§ `Division 5: attributed liability of officers, partners and third parties (ss 236A to 236L)`

@export Under section 236H(1), may the Authority bring an action against me for a civil penalty as an officer, partner or manager of an entity that contravened Part 12?
GIVEN
    `it appears to the Authority that the corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association has contravened a provision of Part 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Authority that a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association (the contravening person) has contravened any provision in Part 12?
    `the person is an officer or member of the corporation, a partner of the partnership, a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership, or an officer or member of the governing body of the unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or (where its affairs are managed by its members) a member of the corporation, a partner of the partnership, a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership, or an officer of the unincorporated association (other than a partnership) or a member of its governing body, as the case may be?
    `the contravention was with the consent or connivance of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention committed with your consent or connivance?
    `the contravention was as a result of neglect on the part of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention as a result of any neglect on your part?
    `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the Authority bringing the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 236H(1), may the Authority bring an action against me for a civil penalty as an officer, partner or manager of an entity that contravened Part 12` IS
    `s 236H(1) the Authority may bring an action in a court against the defendant to seek an order for a civil penalty` `it appears to the Authority that the corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association has contravened a provision of Part 12` `the person is an officer or member of the corporation, a partner of the partnership, a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership, or an officer or member of the governing body of the unincorporated association` `the contravention was with the consent or connivance of the person` `the contravention was as a result of neglect on the part of the person` `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action`

@export Under section 236H(2), what is the most I can be ordered to pay as a civil penalty as an officer, partner or manager, in dollars?
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that you gained as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that you avoided as a result of the contravention? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 236H(2), what is the most I can be ordered to pay as a civil penalty as an officer, partner or manager, in dollars` IS
    `s 236H(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` `the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`

@export Under section 236I(1), am I liable to pay compensation to the claimant as an officer, partner or manager?
GIVEN
    `the defendant is a defendant (the answer under section 236A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for "defendant" in section 236A answer for this defendant? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the defendant has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision of Part 12?
    `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person? (the court takes the matters in section 234(5) into account)
    `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant suffered loss by reason of the difference between (i) the price at which the capital markets products were dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention and (ii) the price at which they would have been likely to have been so dealt in, on the hypothesis that paragraph (b)(ii)(A) or (B) selects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 236I(1), am I liable to pay compensation to the claimant as an officer, partner or manager` IS
    `s 236I(1) the defendant is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` `the defendant is a defendant (the answer under section 236A)` `the defendant has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in`

@export Under section 236L(1), may a court order me to disgorge a benefit as a third party?
GIVEN
    `a person has been convicted by a court of an offence in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person been convicted by a court of an offence in respect of a contravention of any provision in Part 12?
    `a person has had an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against the person under section 232 or Division 5, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person had an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against you under section 232 or any of the provisions in Division 5 by a court, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order made with or without admission of contravention, in respect of a contravention of any provision in Part 12?
    `in an action commenced under section 236L a court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that a contravention of a provision of Part 12 by a person has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In an action commenced under section 236L, is a court satisfied on a balance of probabilities that a contravention by a person of any provision in Part 12 has occurred?
    `the Authority or a claimant has applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority or any claimant applied for the order?
    `the other person has received the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, as the third party, received the whole or any part of the benefit of that contravention?
    `the benefit was derived from trades carried out for the third party by the person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit one derived from trades carried out for you by the person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 236L(1), may a court order me to disgorge a benefit as a third party` IS
    `s 236L(1) the court may make an order against the third party for disgorgement of the benefit` `a person has been convicted by a court of an offence in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part 12` `a person has had an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against the person under section 232 or Division 5, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order` `in an action commenced under section 236L a court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that a contravention of a provision of Part 12 by a person has occurred` `the Authority or a claimant has applied for the order` `the other person has received the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention` `the benefit was derived from trades carried out for the third party by the person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`

@export Under section 236L(4), am I protected against an order for disgorgement, or against disgorgement of the entire benefit?
GIVEN
    `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party acquired the benefit without knowing, and in circumstances such as not to arouse a reasonable suspicion, that it was derived from the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that you acquired the benefit without knowing, and in circumstances such as not to arouse a reasonable suspicion, that the benefit was derived from the contravention referred to in subsection (1)?
    `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party has so altered its position in reliance on an indefeasible interest in the benefit that it would be inequitable to make the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that you have so altered your position in reliance on your having an indefeasible interest in the benefit that, in the opinion of the court, it would be inequitable to make the order for disgorgement, or to order disgorgement of the entire benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 236L(4), am I protected against an order for disgorgement, or against disgorgement of the entire benefit` IS
    `s 236L(4) the court is not to make an order for disgorgement, or not of the entire benefit, against the third party` `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party acquired the benefit without knowing, and in circumstances such as not to arouse a reasonable suspicion, that it was derived from the contravention` `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party has so altered its position in reliance on an indefeasible interest in the benefit that it would be inequitable to make the order`

-- 50 questions.

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sfac (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- THE SEAT LAYER of sfac (Part 13 Division 1 Subdivisions (1) and (2), ss 239 to 260).
--
-- SEAT: an individual who offers, issues, sells or underwrites securities, debentures or units, or who is a director of an entity that does: the offeror's or issuer's or director's questions
-- about whether a prospectus or a profile statement is required, what it must contain, how long it lasts, what may be advertised, and what follows (offences, penalties, liability to investors) if it is not done.
-- There is never a seat for the Authority or the Minister: their powers (stop orders, registration, exemptions) are read here only as facts about the person's own offer.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked, and calls the layer-1 function of the same section; no rule is restated here.
-- A fact the person says is "yes" or "no" is passed to a layer-1 input that wants an answer as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE (the person has stated it); where only JUST TRUE counts for an exemption or an open route,
-- a "no" is passed as NOTHING ("not shown"), never as FALSE.
-- A fact the question does not ask is passed as NOTHING where the layer-1 input is a MAYBE BOOLEAN, which is read there as "not shown".
-- The direction of each question is the direction of the layer-1 function it returns: a bar is asked as "am I barred", a duty as "have I", an offence as "am I guilty", a definition as "is it".
-- Keel concepts used: s 2(1) "director" (the person is a director), computed by the keel's function.

§ `Securities and Futures Act 2001 -- the questions of the person who offers, issues or directs an offer`

§§ `Section 239, 239A and Subdivision (4): does this Subdivision apply to my offer`

@export Under section 239A, section 239(8) and Subdivision (4), does Subdivision (2) apply to my offer?
GIVEN `the date I make the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make (or did you make) the offer?
      `the offer is one to which, but for section 239A, both Division 1 and Division 2 apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer one to which, but for section 239A, both Division 1 and Division 2 of Part 13 apply?
      `the Authority has declared by order in the Gazette that Division 1 does not apply to my offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority declared, by order in the Gazette, that Division 1 of Part 13 does not apply to your offer?
      `my offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer one of units, or derivatives of units, in a business trust?
      `my business trust is also a collective investment scheme authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business trust also a collective investment scheme authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287?
      `my business trust is also a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business trust also a collective investment scheme?
      `my offer is made in reliance on an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the offer in reliance on an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 2 of Part 13?
      `my offer is exempted from Subdivision (2) by a provision of Subdivision (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer exempted from Subdivision (2) by a provision of Subdivision (4) of Division 2?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 239A, section 239(8) and Subdivision (4), does Subdivision (2) apply to my offer` MEANS
    `s 239A(1) and (2), s 239(8) and Subdivision (4): this Subdivision applies to the offer`
        (`s 239(8) this Division applies to the offer` `the date I make the offer`)
        (`s 239A(1) the Authority's declaration disapplies this Division to the offer` `the offer is one to which, but for section 239A, both Division 1 and Division 2 apply` `the Authority has declared by order in the Gazette that Division 1 does not apply to my offer`)
        (`s 239A(2) this Division does not apply to the offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` `my offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` `my business trust is also a collective investment scheme authorised under section 286 or recognised under section 287` `my business trust is also a collective investment scheme` `my offer is made in reliance on an exemption under Subdivision (4) of Division 2`)
        (IF `my offer is exempted from Subdivision (2) by a provision of Subdivision (4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

§§ `Section 240: the prospectus and the profile statement`

@export Under section 240(1), am I barred from making this offer without a registered prospectus or a profile statement?
GIVEN `I make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
      `Subdivision (2) applies to my offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Subdivision (2) of Division 1 of Part 13 apply to your offer (the answer to the question under section 239A, section 239(8) and Subdivision (4))?
      `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus in respect of the offer?
      `my prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus prepared in accordance with section 243?
      `a copy of my prospectus signed as section 240(4A) requires is lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged with the Authority a copy of the prospectus signed in accordance with section 240(4A)?
      `my prospectus is registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus?
      `my offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your offer comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed?
      `my offer is made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 240(1), am I barred from making this offer without a registered prospectus or a profile statement` MEANS
    `s 240(1) the person must not make the offer`
        `I make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
        (IF `Subdivision (2) applies to my offer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus`
        `my prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243`
        `a copy of my prospectus signed as section 240(4A) requires is lodged with the Authority`
        `my prospectus is registered by the Authority`
        `my offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed`
        (IF `my offer is made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 240(7), am I guilty of an offence for making this offer without a registered prospectus or a profile statement?
GIVEN `I make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
      `Subdivision (2) applies to my offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Subdivision (2) of Division 1 of Part 13 apply to your offer (the answer to the question under section 239A, section 239(8) and Subdivision (4))?
      `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus in respect of the offer?
      `my prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus prepared in accordance with section 243?
      `a copy of my prospectus signed as section 240(4A) requires is lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged with the Authority a copy of the prospectus signed in accordance with section 240(4A)?
      `my prospectus is registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered the prospectus?
      `my offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your offer comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed?
      `my offer is made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 240(7), am I guilty of an offence for making this offer without a registered prospectus or a profile statement` MEANS
    `s 240(7) the person is guilty of an offence`
        (`s 240(1) the person must not make the offer`
            `I make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
            (IF `Subdivision (2) applies to my offer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
            `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus`
            `my prospectus is prepared in accordance with section 243`
            `a copy of my prospectus signed as section 240(4A) requires is lodged with the Authority`
            `my prospectus is registered by the Authority`
            `my offer complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed`
            (IF `my offer is made in or accompanied by a profile statement in accordance with section 240(4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING))
        NOTHING

@export Under section 240(7), what is the most I can be fined, in Singapore dollars, for making this offer without a registered prospectus or a profile statement?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 240(7), what is the most I can be fined, in Singapore dollars, for making this offer without a registered prospectus or a profile statement` MEANS
    (`s 240(7) the penalty for the offence`)'s `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`

§§ `Section 240AA: the product highlights sheet`

@export Under section 240AA(1), am I barred from making this offer without a product highlights sheet?
GIVEN `I make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
      `my securities or contracts are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts you offer asset-backed securities, structured notes, or of a kind the Authority has prescribed under section 240AA(5)?
      `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240?
      `my prospectus or profile statement is accompanied by a product highlights sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the prospectus or profile statement accompanied by a product highlights sheet in respect of the offer?
      `my product highlights sheet complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the product highlights sheet comply with the requirements the Authority has prescribed?
      `a copy of my product highlights sheet is lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged a copy of the product highlights sheet with the Authority?
      `I am exempted from the requirements in section 240AA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted you from the requirements in section 240AA, by regulations or by written notice?
      `Subdivision (2) applies to my offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Subdivision (2) of Division 1 of Part 13 apply to your offer (the answer to the question under section 239A, section 239(8) and Subdivision (4))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 240AA(1), am I barred from making this offer without a product highlights sheet` MEANS
    `s 240AA(1) the person must not make the offer`
        `I make an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
        (IF `my securities or contracts are relevant securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement that complies with section 240`
        `my prospectus or profile statement is accompanied by a product highlights sheet`
        `my product highlights sheet complies with the requirements the Authority has prescribed`
        `a copy of my product highlights sheet is lodged with the Authority`
        (IF `I am exempted from the requirements in section 240AA` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `Subdivision (2) applies to my offer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

§§ `Section 241: a supplementary or replacement document`

@export Under section 241(7), have I kept the offer open for at least 14 days after lodging the supplementary or replacement document?
GIVEN `I have lodged a supplementary document or replacement document with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged a supplementary document or a replacement document with the Authority?
      `the date I lodged the supplementary document or replacement document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you lodge it (any date if you have not)?
      `the date until which I keep the offer open` IS A DATE @desc Until what date do you keep the offer open?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 241(7), have I kept the offer open for at least 14 days after lodging the supplementary or replacement document` MEANS
    `s 241(7) the offer has been kept open for at least 14 days after the lodgment` `I have lodged a supplementary document or replacement document with the Authority` `the date I lodged the supplementary document or replacement document` `the date until which I keep the offer open`

§§ `Section 242: a stop order`

@export Under section 242(9), is the interim stop order in force on the date I ask about?
GIVEN `the Authority has revoked the interim stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority revoked the interim stop order?
      `the interim stop order was served during a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interim stop order served during a hearing under section 242(4), or a hearing under section 242(8)?
      `the Authority has made a stop order under section 242(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority made a stop order under section 242(1) or (2)?
      `the day the interim stop order was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the interim stop order served on you?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 242(9), is the interim stop order in force on the date I ask about` MEANS
    `s 242(9) the interim stop order is in force` `the Authority has revoked the interim stop order` `the interim stop order was served during a hearing` `the Authority has made a stop order under section 242(1) or (2)` `the day the interim stop order was served` `the date asked`

@export Under section 242(11), am I barred from allotting, issuing or selling the securities while a stop order is in force?
GIVEN `a stop order or an interim stop order served on me is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a stop order, or an interim stop order, served on you in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 242(11), am I barred from allotting, issuing or selling the securities while a stop order is in force` MEANS
    IF `a stop order or an interim stop order served on me is in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Sections 243 and 245: what the prospectus must contain and over-subscriptions`

@export Under section 243(1), does my prospectus contain what it must contain?
GIVEN `my document is a prospectus for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a prospectus for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
      `my prospectus contains all the information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus contain all the information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters in section 243(3)?
      `my prospectus contains the matters prescribed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus contain the matters the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 243(1), does my prospectus contain what it must contain` MEANS
    `s 243(1) the prospectus contains what it must contain` `my document is a prospectus for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` `my prospectus contains all the information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require` `my prospectus contains the matters prescribed by the Authority`

@export Under section 245(1), am I barred from accepting or retaining subscriptions in excess of the amount of the debenture issue?
GIVEN `I am an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
      `I accept or retain subscriptions to a debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you accept or retain subscriptions to a debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue as disclosed in the prospectus?
      `my prospectus expressly reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus expressly reserve the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions?
      `my prospectus states a limit on the over-subscriptions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus state a limit on the over-subscriptions that may be accepted or retained, expressed as a sum or a percentage?
      `the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus, in dollars?
      `the limit on the over-subscriptions stated in the prospectus` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the limit on the over-subscriptions stated in the prospectus, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 245(1), am I barred from accepting or retaining subscriptions in excess of the amount of the debenture issue` MEANS
    `s 245(1) the entity must not accept or retain the subscriptions` `I am an entity` `I accept or retain subscriptions to a debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus` `my prospectus expressly reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions` `my prospectus states a limit on the over-subscriptions` `the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus` `the limit on the over-subscriptions stated in the prospectus`

§§ `Sections 249 to 252: consents, the life of a prospectus, advertising, notices`

@export Under section 249(1), am I barred from issuing the prospectus without the expert's written consent?
GIVEN `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement?
      `my prospectus or profile statement includes a statement made by, or based on a statement made by, an expert` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement include a statement purporting to be made by, or based on a statement made by, an expert?
      `the Authority has exempted me or my prospectus from section 249` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted you, or the prospectus or profile statement, or a class it belongs to, from section 249?
      `the expert has given written consent and not withdrawn it before registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the expert given written consent to the issue of the prospectus or profile statement with the statement included, and not withdrawn it before the registration?
      `my prospectus says the expert has given and not withdrawn consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement say that the expert has given, and has not withdrawn, the consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 249(1), am I barred from issuing the prospectus without the expert's written consent` MEANS
    `s 249(1) the prospectus or profile statement must not be issued`
        `my offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement`
        `my prospectus or profile statement includes a statement made by, or based on a statement made by, an expert`
        (`s 249(3) the person or document is exempt from the section` `the Authority has exempted me or my prospectus from section 249`)
        `the expert has given written consent and not withdrawn it before registration`
        `my prospectus says the expert has given and not withdrawn consent`

@export Under section 250(3), what is the last day on which I may offer, allot, issue or sell on this prospectus?
GIVEN `my securities are debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities debentures, or units of debentures, issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A?
      `the date the Authority registered the base prospectus or prospectus` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Authority register the base prospectus (for a debenture issuance programme) or the prospectus?
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 250(3), what is the last day on which I may offer, allot, issue or sell on this prospectus` MEANS
    `s 250(3) the last day of the period` `my securities are debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A` `the date the Authority registered the base prospectus or prospectus`

@export Under section 250(1), am I barred from offering, allotting, issuing or selling on this prospectus on the date I ask about?
GIVEN `I make an offer, or allot, issue or sell, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an offer, or allot, issue or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement?
      `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `my securities are debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities debentures, or units of debentures, issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A?
      `the date the Authority registered the base prospectus or prospectus` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Authority register the base prospectus (for a debenture issuance programme) or the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 250(1), am I barred from offering, allotting, issuing or selling on this prospectus on the date I ask about` MEANS
    `s 250(1) the person must not make the offer or allot, issue or sell on the basis of the prospectus`
        `I make an offer, or allot, issue or sell, on the basis of a prospectus or profile statement`
        `the date asked`
        (`s 250(3) the last day of the period` `my securities are debentures issued under a debenture issuance programme under section 240A` `the date the Authority registered the base prospectus or prospectus`)

@export Under section 251(1), am I barred from advertising this offer or publishing a statement about it?
GIVEN `a prospectus is required for my offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a prospectus required for your offer or intended offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
      `I advertise the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you advertise the offer or intended offer?
      `I publish a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you publish a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer?
      `I publish a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you publish a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
      `my advertisement or publication is authorised by section 251` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement or publication one that section 251 authorises (for example a notice that meets section 251(6) before registration, or section 251(8) after it)?
      `the Authority has exempted me from section 251` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted you, or a class of persons you belong to, from section 251?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 251(1), am I barred from advertising this offer or publishing a statement about it` MEANS
    `s 251(1) the person must not advertise the offer or publish the statement`
        `a prospectus is required for my offer or intended offer`
        `I advertise the offer or intended offer`
        `I publish a statement that directly or indirectly refers to the offer or intended offer`
        `I publish a statement that is reasonably likely to induce persons to subscribe for or purchase the securities or contracts`
        (IF `my advertisement or publication is authorised by section 251` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
        (`s 251(14) the person is exempt from this section` `the Authority has exempted me from section 251`)

@export Under section 252(1), have I notified the person making the offer as I must?
GIVEN `I am a person referred to in section 254(3) other than paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person referred to in section 254(3), other than paragraph (a) (for example a director of the entity, an issue manager or an underwriter named in the prospectus)?
      `I become aware after the registration but before the close of the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you become aware, at any time after the prospectus or profile statement is registered but before the close of the offer, of any of the matters in section 252(1)(a), (b) or (c)?
      `a statement in the prospectus or profile statement is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement in the prospectus or the profile statement false or misleading?
      `there is an omission of information required by section 243 or 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243, or in the profile statement under section 246?
      `a new circumstance has arisen since lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a new circumstance arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
      `the new circumstance would have been required had it arisen before lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the new circumstance have been required to be included in the prospectus under section 243, or in the profile statement under section 246, if it had arisen before lodgment?
      `my failure to notify would have been materially adverse from the point of view of an investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a failure by you to notify have been materially adverse from the point of view of an investor?
      `I have notified the person making the offer in writing as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the person making the offer, in writing, as soon as practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 252(1), have I notified the person making the offer as I must` MEANS
    `s 252(1) the person has notified the person making the offer`
        `I am a person referred to in section 254(3) other than paragraph (a)`
        `I become aware after the registration but before the close of the offer`
        `a statement in the prospectus or profile statement is false or misleading`
        `there is an omission of information required by section 243 or 246`
        `a new circumstance has arisen since lodgment`
        `the new circumstance would have been required had it arisen before lodgment`
        `my failure to notify would have been materially adverse from the point of view of an investor`
        `I have notified the person making the offer in writing as soon as practicable`

§§ `Sections 253 to 255: false or misleading statements, and the defence`

@export Under section 253(1), am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, the prospectus, as a director of the entity making the offer?
GIVEN `an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus or profile statement?
      `the offer is an offer referred to in section 280` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer referred to in section 280?
      `a prospectus or profile statement is prepared and issued in relation to the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a prospectus or profile statement prepared and issued in relation to the offer?
      `a false or misleading statement is contained in the prospectus, the profile statement or an application form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a false or misleading statement contained in the prospectus, the profile statement or an application form for the securities or contracts?
      `there is an omission of information required by section 243 or 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission to state any information required to be included in the prospectus under section 243, or in the profile statement under section 246?
      `a new circumstance has been omitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission to state a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or the profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
      `the omitted new circumstance would have been required had it arisen before lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the new circumstance have been required to be included, had it arisen before lodgment?
      `the statement or omission is not materially adverse from the point of view of the investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the false or misleading statement, or the omission, not materially adverse from the point of view of the investor?
      `the person making the offer is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer an entity?
      `I am a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
      `I am the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person making the offer?
      `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your liability be only because of a false or misleading statement in the prospectus or profile statement (and not for an omission)?
      `I made all reasonable inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you made all inquiries (if any) that were reasonable in the circumstances?
      `I believed on reasonable grounds that the statement was not false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that, after doing so, you believed on reasonable grounds that the statement was not false or misleading?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 253(1), am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading statement in, or an omission from, the prospectus, as a director of the entity making the offer` MEANS
    `s 253(1) the person is guilty of an offence`
        (`s 253(1) the false or misleading statement or omission is present` `an offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` `the offer is an offer referred to in section 280` `a prospectus or profile statement is prepared and issued in relation to the offer` `a false or misleading statement is contained in the prospectus, the profile statement or an application form` `there is an omission of information required by section 243 or 246` `a new circumstance has been omitted` `the omitted new circumstance would have been required had it arisen before lodgment`)
        (`s 253(3) the person does not contravene subsection (1)` `the statement or omission is not materially adverse from the point of view of the investor`)
        (`s 253(4) the person is one of the persons guilty of the offence` `I am the person making the offer`
            (`s 253(4)(b) the person is a director or proposed director of the entity making the offer` `the person making the offer is an entity` (`s 2(1) "director" the person is a director` `I am a director of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE)
            NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)
        (`s 255 the person has a defence`
            (`s 255(1) this section gives a defence for the false or misleading statement` (`I am the person making the offer` OR `I am a director of the corporation`) `the liability is only because of a false or misleading statement` `I made all reasonable inquiries` `I believed on reasonable grounds that the statement was not false or misleading`)
            NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING)

@export Under section 253(1), what is the most I can be fined, in Singapore dollars, for a false or misleading statement in the prospectus?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 253(1), what is the most I can be fined, in Singapore dollars, for a false or misleading statement in the prospectus` MEANS
    (`s 253(1) the penalty for the offence`)'s `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars`

§§ `Sections 258 and 259: application moneys and listing`

@export Under section 258(1), have I held the applicants' moneys on trust in a separate bank account until allotment?
GIVEN `the moneys are application or other moneys paid before allotment on account of securities offered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the moneys application or other moneys paid by an applicant before allotment on account of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts you offered?
      `the allotment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the allotment of the securities or contracts been made?
      `I hold the moneys upon trust for the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold the moneys upon trust for the applicant?
      `the moneys are in a separate bank account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the moneys in a separate bank account?
      `the bank account is kept solely for the applicants' moneys for these securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the bank account one you established and keep solely for depositing the moneys paid by applicants for those securities or contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 258(1), have I held the applicants' moneys on trust in a separate bank account until allotment` MEANS
    `s 258(1) the person making the offer holds the moneys on trust in a separate bank account` `the moneys are application or other moneys paid before allotment on account of securities offered` `the allotment has been made` `I hold the moneys upon trust for the applicant` `the moneys are in a separate bank account` `the bank account is kept solely for the applicants' moneys for these securities`

@export Under section 259(1), was permission to list the securities not applied for, or not granted, in time?
GIVEN `my prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made to list the securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus state or imply that application has been or will be made for permission to list the securities or contracts for quotation on an approved exchange?
      `the date my prospectus was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the prospectus issued?
      `permission was applied for in the form required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was permission applied for in the form required by the approved exchange?
      `the date permission was applied for` IS A DATE @desc On what date was permission applied for (any date if it was not)?
      `permission was granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was permission granted?
      `the date permission was granted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was permission granted (any date if it was not)?
      `the weeks of a longer period notified within the 6 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks is the longer period the approved exchange notified within the 6 weeks (0 if none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 259(1), was permission to list the securities not applied for, or not granted, in time` MEANS
    `s 259(1) the permission was not applied for or not granted in time`
        (`s 259(1)(a) the permission was not applied for in time` `my prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made to list the securities` `the date my prospectus was issued` `permission was applied for in the form required` `the date permission was applied for`)
        (`s 259(1)(b) the permission was not granted in time` `my prospectus states or implies that application has been or will be made to list the securities` `the date my prospectus was issued` `permission was granted` `the date permission was granted` `the weeks of a longer period notified within the 6 weeks`)

§§ `Section 260: the minimum subscription`

@export Under section 260(1), am I barred from making this allotment?
GIVEN `I make an allotment of securities or contracts of a company or business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an allotment of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a company or business trust?
      `the minimum subscription has been subscribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the minimum subscription been subscribed?
      `the sum payable on application has been received by cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum payable on application been received by cheque?
      `the cheque has been paid by the bank on which it is drawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the cheque been paid by the bank on which it is drawn?
      `the sum payable on application has been received otherwise than by cheque` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sum payable on application been received otherwise than by cheque?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 260(1), am I barred from making this allotment` MEANS
    `s 260(1) the person must not make the allotment` `I make an allotment of securities or contracts of a company or business trust` `the minimum subscription has been subscribed` (`s 260(1A) the sum payable on application is treated as received` `the sum payable on application has been received by cheque` `the cheque has been paid by the bank on which it is drawn` `the sum payable on application has been received otherwise than by cheque`)

@export Under section 260(3), is the amount payable on application at least 5% of the price?
GIVEN `the price at which each share, debenture or unit is or will be offered` IS A NUMBER @desc At what price, in dollars, is each share, debenture, unit or derivative of a unit offered?
      `the amount payable on application on each` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, is payable on application on each?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 260(3), is the amount payable on application at least 5% of the price` MEANS
    `s 260(3) the amount payable on application is not less than 5% of the price` `the price at which each share, debenture or unit is or will be offered` `the amount payable on application on each`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part sfad (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 2, part sfad: THE SEAT LAYER for Part 13 Division 1 Subdivisions (3), (4) and (5), ss 261 to 282AA.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who issues, offers, holds or deals in securities, debentures or units, or who is an officer
-- (a director or equivalent person of a borrowing entity, a guarantor entity or an offeror; a trustee for debenture holders)
-- or a substantial shareholder, asking, on facts they can state, what the Act requires of them or lets them do, what an offer needs
-- (a prospectus or a stated exemption) and what follows if it is not done. There is never a seat for the Authority, the Minister or the Court:
-- their powers appear here only as what they mean to the individual (sections 281(2) and 282AA(2) to (5)).
--
-- Every question names its section ("Under section N, ...") and asks in the direction its body answers: a question that asks "may I", "is it exempt",
-- "must I" calls a function whose JUST TRUE means yes; a question that asks "am I barred" or "am I guilty" calls the bar or the offence.
-- Every question calls the layer-1 rules and never restates one. Every input is a plain fact the person can state, with a @desc worded as they would be asked;
-- where a layer-1 function takes the answer of another section's function, the question calls that function with the person's facts and passes its answer on.
-- A plain yes or no is passed to a function that takes a MAYBE BOOLEAN as JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE (the person says what they know; a person who does not know
-- should not use the question).
--
-- What the seat leaves out, and why: section 272A(1) as a whole, section 272B(1) as a whole, section 273(1) as a whole and the section 275(1A) route are asked
-- limb by limb (the whole conjunction needs thirty or more facts and the limbs are what a person can answer); section 277(1) is asked for an offer of shares
-- or other securities issued by a listed corporation (sub-paragraph (a)(ii)); the Authority's own decisions (ss 261(1C)(a) and (b), 266, 267, 277(1AB),
-- 277(1AD), 277(2), 280A, 281(1), 282AA(1)) are not asked from the individual's side.


§ `Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (3): debentures`


§§ `Section 261: the prescribed entity and its conditions`

@export Under section 261(1D), am I guilty of an offence if I contravene a condition or restriction the Authority imposed on a prescribed entity?
GIVEN `I contravene a condition or restriction the Authority imposed on the prescribed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you contravened a condition or restriction that the Authority imposed on a prescribed entity by written notice under section 261(1C)(a)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 261(1D), am I guilty of an offence for contravening a condition or restriction imposed on a prescribed entity` MEANS
    `s 261(1D) the person is guilty of an offence` `I contravene a condition or restriction the Authority imposed on the prescribed entity`


§§ `Section 262: asset-backed securities`

@export Under section 262(3), are the securities I hold asset-backed securities?
GIVEN `the arrangement involves selling, transferring or assigning assets to a special purpose vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the arrangement the securities were issued under involve the sale, transfer or assignment of assets to a special purpose vehicle?
      `the sale, transfer or assignment is funded by issuing debentures or units of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that sale, transfer or assignment funded by the issue of debentures or units of debentures (by that vehicle or another special purpose vehicle)?
      `payments on those debentures come principally from the cash flows of the assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are payments on those debentures or units of debentures, or will they be, principally derived (directly or indirectly) from the cash flows generated by the assets?
      `my securities are debentures or units of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities you hold debentures or units of debentures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 262(3), are the securities I hold asset-backed securities` MEANS
    `s 262(3) the securities are asset-backed securities` `my securities are debentures or units of debentures` (`s 262(3) the arrangement is a securitisation transaction` `the arrangement involves selling, transferring or assigning assets to a special purpose vehicle` `the sale, transfer or assignment is funded by issuing debentures or units of debentures` `payments on those debentures come principally from the cash flows of the assets`)


§§ `Section 265A: the trustee for the holders of debentures`

@export Under section 265A(1), must the borrowing entity appoint a trustee for the holders of its debentures for the entire tenure?
GIVEN `an offer of debentures is made in or accompanied by a prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer of debentures made in, or accompanied by, a prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 265A(1), must the borrowing entity appoint a trustee for the holders of its debentures` MEANS
    `s 265A(1) the borrowing entity must appoint a trustee for the holders of debentures for the entire tenure` `an offer of debentures is made in or accompanied by a prospectus`

@export Under section 265A(4), am I guilty of an offence for contravening section 265A(1), (2) or (3)?
GIVEN `I contravene section 265A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contravene section 265A(1) (no trustee appointed for the holders of the debentures for the entire tenure)?
      `I contravene section 265A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contravene section 265A(2) (the trustee appointed does not meet the requirements)?
      `I contravene section 265A(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contravene section 265A(3) (you did not consider the matters before being satisfied the trustee is suitable)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 265A(4), am I guilty of an offence for contravening section 265A(1), (2) or (3)` MEANS
    `s 265A(4) the person is guilty of an offence` `I contravene section 265A(1)` `I contravene section 265A(2)` `I contravene section 265A(3)`


§§ `Section 268: the borrowing entity's accounts and particulars`

@export Under section 268(6)(a), did I lodge the half-year accounts with the trustee in time?
GIVEN `the first 6 months of the financial year ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the first 6 months of the financial year end?
      `I lodged the accounts with the trustee on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge the accounts with the trustee?
      `the accounts are a profit and loss account for the first 6 months and a balance sheet at their end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the accounts a profit and loss account for the first 6 months and a balance sheet as at the end of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 268(6)(a), did I lodge the half-year accounts with the trustee in time` MEANS
    `s 268(6)(a) the half-year accounts are made out and lodged in time` `the first 6 months of the financial year ended on` `I lodged the accounts with the trustee on` `the accounts are a profit and loss account for the first 6 months and a balance sheet at their end`

@export Under section 268(6)(b), did I lodge the annual accounts with the trustee in time?
GIVEN `the financial year ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the financial year end?
      `I lodged the accounts with the trustee on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge the accounts with the trustee?
      `the accounts are a profit and loss account for the financial year and a balance sheet at its end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the accounts a profit and loss account for the financial year and a balance sheet as at the end of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 268(6)(b), did I lodge the annual accounts with the trustee in time` MEANS
    `s 268(6)(b) the annual accounts are made out and lodged in time` `the financial year ended on` `I lodged the accounts with the trustee on` `the accounts are a profit and loss account for the financial year and a balance sheet at its end`

@export Under section 268(7), am I guilty of an offence for failing to comply with section 268(6)?
GIVEN `I fail to comply with section 268(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as a director or equivalent person of the borrowing entity, fail to comply with section 268(6) (to cause the accounts to be made out and lodged with the trustee)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 268(7), am I guilty of an offence for failing to comply with section 268(6)` MEANS
    `s 268(7) the person is guilty of an offence` `I fail to comply with section 268(6)`


§§ `Section 268A: the semi-annual report`

@export Under section 268A(2), was the semi-annual report lodged with the trustee in time?
GIVEN `the 6 months covered by the report ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the period of 6 months covered by the semi-annual report end?
      `I lodged the report with the trustee on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge the semi-annual report with the trustee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
